window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["rag-llamaindex"]=[{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0001","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-001-overview","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s001","q":"Which tools and versions does the RAG with LlamaIndex course use?","a":"<p>LlamaIndex 0.10.x, Qdrant as the vector database, and Cohere and OpenAI as the LLM and embedding providers.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0002","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-001-overview","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s001","q":"What is the course project of the RAG with LlamaIndex course?","a":"<p>A chatbot grounded in philosophers' books.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0003","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-002-1-rag-overview-use-cases","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s002","q":"What is Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG)?","a":"<p>RAG enhances an LLM by connecting it to external data stores, including private datasets.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0004","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-002-1-rag-overview-use-cases","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s002","q":"What are the three steps of RAG?","a":"<ol>\n  <li><strong>Retrieve</strong> context from an external source.</li>\n  <li><strong>Augment</strong> the prompt with it.</li>\n  <li><strong>Generate</strong> the answer with the LLM.</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0005","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-002-1-rag-overview-use-cases","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s002","q":"Why do LLMs give stale information, and how does RAG help?","a":"<p>LLMs are trained on static internet scrapes. RAG retrieves current data from external stores and injects it into the context window.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0006","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-002-1-rag-overview-use-cases","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s002","q":"Why do LLMs give no source attribution, and how does RAG help?","a":"<p>Their knowledge is baked into the weights. With RAG, the answer can be traced back to the retrieved documents.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0007","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-002-1-rag-overview-use-cases","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s002","q":"Why do LLMs hallucinate, and how does RAG help?","a":"<p>They are trained for natural-sounding language, not truthfulness. With RAG, grounding data can be added, updated or deleted in real time.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0008","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-002-1-rag-overview-use-cases","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s002","q":"Why do LLMs give generic answers, and how does RAG help?","a":"<p>They have no domain data. RAG lets you plug in domain-specific data.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0009","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-002-1-rag-overview-use-cases","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s002","q":"How do you load documents from a directory in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Use <code>SimpleDirectoryReader</code> and call <code>load_data()</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from llama_index.core import VectorStoreIndex, SimpleDirectoryReader\ndocuments = SimpleDirectoryReader(&quot;./data&quot;).load_data()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0010","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-002-1-rag-overview-use-cases","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s002","q":"How do you create an index (embeddings plus vector store) from documents in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Call <code>VectorStoreIndex.from_documents</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>index = VectorStoreIndex.from_documents(documents)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0011","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-002-1-rag-overview-use-cases","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s002","q":"How do you query a LlamaIndex index so it retrieves context and sends it to the LLM?","a":"<p>Turn the index into a query engine and call <code>query</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query_engine = index.as_query_engine()\nresponse = query_engine.query(&quot;What are the key themes in these documents?&quot;)\nprint(response)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0012","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-002-1-rag-overview-use-cases","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s002","q":"In the minimal LlamaIndex RAG example, which code does each RAG step map to?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Retrieve</strong>: load documents with <code>SimpleDirectoryReader(\"./data\").load_data()</code>.</li>\n  <li><strong>Augment</strong>: create the index with <code>VectorStoreIndex.from_documents(documents)</code>.</li>\n  <li><strong>Generate</strong>: query with <code>index.as_query_engine()</code> and <code>query(...)</code>.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0013","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-003-use-cases","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s003","q":"What is the canonical use case of RAG, and how does the code change for it?","a":"<p>Q&amp;A over private data such as internal docs, papers and proprietary data. The code is the same, with <code>SimpleDirectoryReader(\"./company_docs\")</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0014","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-003-use-cases","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s003","q":"Which RAG use cases are mentioned besides Q&amp;A over private data?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Customer support chatbots: real-time, accurate answers from updated data.</li>\n  <li>Healthcare / medical research and legal research: fast access to current guidelines, case law and statutes.</li>\n  <li>Generative search and conversational interfaces (for example Perplexity AI): cited answers instead of link lists.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0015","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-003-use-cases","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s003","q":"How do you build a customer support chatbot with chat memory in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Create a chat engine with <code>chat_mode=\"condense_question\"</code> and call <code>chat</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>chat_engine = index.as_chat_engine(chat_mode=&quot;condense_question&quot;)\nresponse = chat_engine.chat(&quot;How do I reset my password?&quot;)\nprint(response)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0016","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-003-use-cases","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s003","q":"How does a LlamaIndex chat engine handle a follow-up question?","a":"<p>It maintains context, so you simply call <code>chat</code> again.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>response = chat_engine.chat(&quot;What if that doesn&#x27;t work?&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0017","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-003-use-cases","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s003","q":"Which LlamaIndex class returns answers with citations, and how do you create it?","a":"<p><code>CitationQueryEngine</code>, created with <code>from_args</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from llama_index.core.query_engine import CitationQueryEngine\nquery_engine = CitationQueryEngine.from_args(index, citation_chunk_size=512)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0018","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-003-use-cases","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s003","q":"How do you list the source nodes behind a cited answer in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Loop over <code>response.source_nodes</code> and print the file name and the start of the text.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for source in response.source_nodes:\n    print(f&quot;- {source.node.metadata.get(&#x27;file_name&#x27;, &#x27;Unknown&#x27;)}: {source.text[:100]}...&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0019","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-003-use-cases","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s003","q":"What does the philosopher chatbot of the course use?","a":"<p>The same chat-engine pattern, with <code>./philosopher_texts</code> and <code>os.environ[\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"]</code> set.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0020","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-004-environment","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s004","q":"Where can you run the RAG with LlamaIndex course?","a":"<p>In <strong>GitHub Codespaces</strong> (a browser dev environment with no local setup, consistent across the team, pick the 4-core/16 GB machine), locally, or in Google Colab, where each notebook pins its installs in the first cell.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0021","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-004-environment","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s004","q":"How do you create the conda environment for the course?","a":"<p>Create it with Python 3.10 and <code>python-dotenv</code>, then activate it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>conda create --name lil_llama_index python==3.10 python-dotenv -y\nconda activate lil_llama_index</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0022","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-004-environment","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s004","q":"Which Jupyter packages does the course install in the conda environment, and how do you check the version?","a":"<p><code>ipykernel</code>, <code>jupyter</code> and <code>jupyterlab</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>conda install ipykernel jupyter jupyterlab -y\njupyter lab --version</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0023","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-004-environment","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s004","q":"Which core libraries does the course install, and why pin versions?","a":"<p>LlamaIndex changes often while the patterns stay the same, so versions are pinned.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pip install llama-index==0.10.37\npip install qdrant-client==1.9.1\npip install llama-index-vector-stores-qdrant==0.2.8 llama-index-readers-file==0.1.22</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0024","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-004-environment","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s004","q":"Which provider packages does the course install for Cohere and OpenAI?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pip install cohere==5.5.0\npip install openai==1.30.1\npip install llama-index-llms-cohere==0.2.0\npip install llama-index-llms-openai==0.1.19\npip install llama-index-embeddings-cohere==0.1.8\npip install llama-index-embeddings-openai==0.1.9\npip install llama-index-postprocessor-cohere-rerank==0.1.6</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0025","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-004-environment","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s004","q":"How do you link the Jupyter kernel to the conda environment (local only)?","a":"<p>Run <code>ipykernel install</code> with the environment name and a display name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>python -m ipykernel install --user --name=lil_llama_index --display-name &quot;LlamaIndex (LinkedIn Learning)&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0026","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-004-environment","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s004","q":"What does <code>01_Getting_Started/install.sh</code> do, and how do you run it?","a":"<p>It automates the setup: it checks that conda exists, creates the env, installs the packages and links the kernel. Run it with <code>chmod +x install.sh &amp;&amp; ./install.sh</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0027","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-004-environment","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s004","q":"What is the purpose of each library in the course install?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Library</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>llama-index</code></td><td>RAG framework (starter package)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>qdrant-client</code>, <code>llama-index-vector-stores-qdrant</code></td><td>Vector DB client and LlamaIndex integration</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>llama-index-readers-file</code></td><td>Load PDFs, DOCX, etc.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>llama-index-llms-openai</code> / <code>-cohere</code></td><td>GPT-4o / Command R+</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>llama-index-embeddings-openai</code> / <code>-cohere</code></td><td>Embedding models</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>llama-index-postprocessor-cohere-rerank</code></td><td>Cohere reranker</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0028","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-004-environment","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s004","q":"Which API keys go into the <code>.env</code> file of the course, and what must you do with <code>.env</code>?","a":"<p><code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code>, <code>CO_API_KEY</code>, <code>QDRANT_API_KEY</code> and <code>QDRANT_URL</code>. Add <code>.env</code> to <code>.gitignore</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>OPENAI_API_KEY=&lt;your-openai-key&gt;\nCO_API_KEY=&lt;your-cohere-key&gt;\nQDRANT_API_KEY=&lt;your-qdrant-api-key&gt;\nQDRANT_URL=&lt;your-qdrant-cluster-url&gt;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0029","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-004-environment","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s004","q":"How do you create the <code>.env</code> file from the shell?","a":"<p>Touch the file, then append each key with <code>echo</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>touch .env\necho &#x27;OPENAI_API_KEY=&lt;your-openai-key&gt;&#x27; &gt;&gt; .env\necho &#x27;CO_API_KEY=&lt;your-cohere-key&gt;&#x27; &gt;&gt; .env</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0030","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-004-environment","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s004","q":"Which extra keys does the repo's <code>.env_example</code> list?","a":"<p><code>MISTRAL_API_KEY</code> and <code>LANGCHAIN_API_KEY</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0031","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-004-environment","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s004","q":"How do you verify the LlamaIndex and Qdrant installation?","a":"<p>Print the version of each library.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import llama_index\nprint(f&quot;LlamaIndex version: {llama_index.core.__version__}&quot;)\nimport qdrant_client\nprint(f&quot;Qdrant client version: {qdrant_client.__version__}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0032","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-004-environment","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s004","q":"How do you load environment variables in a notebook and check that the keys are set?","a":"<p>Call <code>load_dotenv()</code>, then check each key with <code>os.getenv</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from dotenv import load_dotenv\nimport os\n\nload_dotenv()\nprint(&quot;OpenAI key loaded:&quot;, bool(os.getenv(&quot;OPENAI_API_KEY&quot;)))\nprint(&quot;Cohere key loaded:&quot;, bool(os.getenv(&quot;CO_API_KEY&quot;)))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0033","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-005-choosing-an-llm-embeddings-provider","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s005","q":"Which LLM providers build and serve their own models, and which host open-source models via API?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Build and serve their own models: OpenAI, Anthropic, Cohere, Mistral, Google Gemini.</li>\n  <li>Host open-source models via API: Fireworks AI, Together AI, Hugging Face, Replicate.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0034","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-005-choosing-an-llm-embeddings-provider","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s005","q":"What is the pattern to install and create an LLM from any provider in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Install <code>llama-index-llms-&lt;provider&gt;</code>, import the provider class and pass the key and the model.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pip install llama-index-llms-&lt;whatever-llm-provider-you-choose&gt;</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from llama_index.llms.&lt;whatever-llm-provider-you-choose&gt; import LLMSProviderClass\n\nllm = LLMSProviderClass(api_key=your_api_key, model=&quot;whatever-model-you-want-to-use&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0035","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-005-choosing-an-llm-embeddings-provider","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s005","q":"Which providers does the course use, and for which half?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Models</th><th>Used</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Cohere</strong></td><td>Command-R, Command-R+</td><td>First half of course</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>OpenAI</strong></td><td>GPT-4o</td><td>Second half</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0036","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-005-choosing-an-llm-embeddings-provider","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s005","q":"What are the limits of the Cohere free trial key?","a":"<p>5 requests per minute, 100 requests per hour and 1000 requests per month.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0037","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-005-choosing-an-llm-embeddings-provider","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s005","q":"What does OpenAI GPT-4o cost in the course, and what are its rate limits?","a":"<p>About $10 per million tokens blended ($5 in, $15 out). Rate limits are tiered (Free, Tier 1 to 5).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0038","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-005-choosing-an-llm-embeddings-provider","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s005","q":"What are the criteria for selecting an LLM provider?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Business objective and use case.</li>\n  <li>Tested capability (accuracy, relevance).</li>\n  <li><strong>License</strong>: commercial vs non-commercial, attribution. Mistral is the most permissive.</li>\n  <li>Language support.</li>\n  <li>Security and privacy (encryption, GDPR/HIPAA).</li>\n  <li>Cost and latency.</li>\n  <li>Community and support.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0039","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-005-choosing-an-llm-embeddings-provider","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s005","q":"Which LLM provider has the most permissive license in the course?","a":"<p>Mistral.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0040","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-005-choosing-an-llm-embeddings-provider","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s005","q":"How do you get the OpenAI and Cohere API keys?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>OpenAI</strong>: platform.openai.com, then API Keys, then Create new secret key. It is shown once.</li>\n  <li><strong>Cohere</strong>: dashboard, then API Key. You can view it later. Never commit keys.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0041","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-006-choosing-a-vector-database","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s006","q":"What are the criteria for choosing a vector database?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Similarity search performance (cosine, Euclidean).</li>\n  <li>Horizontal scalability.</li>\n  <li>Framework integration (LlamaIndex, LangChain).</li>\n  <li>Data types supported.</li>\n  <li>Incremental and real-time indexing.</li>\n  <li>Retrieval flexibility (top-k, thresholds, metadata filters).</li>\n  <li>Persistence and recovery.</li>\n  <li>Community and docs.</li>\n  <li>Ease of deployment (cloud or on-prem).</li>\n  <li>Cost and license.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0042","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-006-choosing-a-vector-database","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s006","q":"Why does the course use Qdrant?","a":"<p>It is popular on LlamaHub, has clear docs and open development, has built-in auth in the dev version, and has a generous free hosted tier (4 GB disk, 1 GB RAM, 1 cluster with multiple collections).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0043","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-006-choosing-a-vector-database","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s006","q":"How do you set up Qdrant Cloud?","a":"<p>Sign in, create a cluster (<code>lil_llama_index</code>), copy the API key immediately (it is not viewable again), copy the cluster URL, and put both in <code>.env</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0044","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-006-choosing-a-vector-database","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s006","q":"How do you connect to Qdrant Cloud and list collections?","a":"<p>Create a <code>QdrantClient</code> with the URL and API key from the environment, then call <code>get_collections</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>client = QdrantClient(\n    url=os.getenv(&quot;QDRANT_URL&quot;),\n    api_key=os.getenv(&quot;QDRANT_API_KEY&quot;)\n)\n\nprint(client.get_collections())</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0045","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-007-course-data-philosopher-books","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s007","q":"Which books does the RAG with LlamaIndex course use as data?","a":"<p>Naval Ravikant's <em>Almanack</em>, <em>Anthology of Balaji</em>, <em>Tao of Seneca</em> vols 1-3, Taleb's <em>Skin in the Game</em>, Paul Graham's <em>Hackers and Painters</em>, and Bruce Lee's <em>Striking Thoughts</em>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0046","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-007-course-data-philosopher-books","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s007","q":"Why do the course books need data cleaning?","a":"<p>All of them are PDFs, so real-world data cleaning (parse, clean, ingest) is part of the work.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0047","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-007-course-data-philosopher-books","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s007","q":"How does the <code>download_file</code> helper save a file?","a":"<p>It builds the destination path <code>../data/&lt;filename&gt;</code>, makes sure the directory exists, downloads the URL, raises an exception on failure, and writes the bytes.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>destination = Path(&#x27;../data&#x27;) / filename\ndestination.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)  # Ensure the directory exists\nresponse = requests.get(url)\nresponse.raise_for_status()  # Raise an exception if the request was unsuccessful\nwith open(destination, &#x27;wb&#x27;) as f:\n    f.write(response.content)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0048","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-007-course-data-philosopher-books","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s007","q":"How do you download the Seneca volumes with <code>download_file</code>?","a":"<p>Loop over a list of URLs and use the last part of each URL as the file name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for url in letters_urls:\n    filename = Path(url).name\n    download_file(url, filename)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0049","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-007-course-data-philosopher-books","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s007","q":"Which file names do the other books use with <code>download_file</code>?","a":"<p>They use the identical <code>download_file(url, \"&lt;name&gt;.pdf\")</code> call with their own URLs: <code>anthology_of_balaji.pdf</code>, <code>skin_in_the_game.pdf</code>, <code>hackers_and_painters.pdf</code> and <code>striking-thoughts.pdf</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0050","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-008-3-llamaindex-fundamentals","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s008","q":"What is LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>A data framework for context-augmented LLM apps (LLM plus private or domain data). It has Python and TypeScript SDKs, and the course uses Python.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0051","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-008-3-llamaindex-fundamentals","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s008","q":"What are the main capabilities of LlamaIndex?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Capability</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Data connectors (Readers)</td><td>Ingest from APIs, PDFs, SQL, etc.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Indexes</td><td>Intermediate data structures optimized for LLM retrieval</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Query engines</td><td>Retrieval interface that returns a synthesized answer</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Chat engines</td><td>Multi-turn conversational interface over your data</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Data agents</td><td>LLM-powered workers augmented with tools</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0052","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-008-3-llamaindex-fundamentals","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s008","q":"What are the three kinds of LlamaIndex packages?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>llama-index-core</code>: loading, indexing, querying, evaluating, with no integrations.</li>\n  <li><strong>Integrations</strong>: LLMs, embeddings, vector stores and readers, each installed separately.</li>\n  <li><strong>Llama Packs</strong>: community templates, often implementing techniques from papers.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0053","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-008-3-llamaindex-fundamentals","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s008","q":"What is LlamaHub?","a":"<p>LlamaHub (llamahub.ai) catalogs all LlamaIndex integrations and packs: 150+ data loaders, 35+ agent tools, 50+ packs, 50+ LLMs, 25+ embeddings and 40+ vector stores. Sort packs by downloads to find the popular ones.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0054","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-008-3-llamaindex-fundamentals","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s008","q":"How do you set the global LLM and embedding model in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Assign them on <code>Settings</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Settings.llm = OpenAI(model=&quot;gpt-4o&quot;)\nSettings.embed_model = OpenAIEmbedding(model=&quot;text-embedding-3-small&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0055","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-008-3-llamaindex-fundamentals","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s008","q":"What is the LlamaIndex pipeline from data to response?","a":"<p>Your data, then a Reader, then an Index (backed by a vector store such as Qdrant), then a Query or Chat engine, then the LLM, then the response.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0056","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-009-3-1-using-llms","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s009","q":"At which two stages does LlamaIndex use LLMs?","a":"<p><strong>Indexing</strong> (judge relevance, summarize) and <strong>querying</strong> (retrieval: fetch data, choose a source, use tools; then response synthesis).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0057","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-009-3-1-using-llms","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s009","q":"What is the notebook setup used by every course notebook?","a":"<p>Import <code>os</code>, <code>getpass</code>, <code>nest_asyncio</code> and <code>dotenv</code>, apply <code>nest_asyncio</code>, load the env, and read the Cohere key.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>nest_asyncio.apply()\nload_dotenv()\nCO_API_KEY = os.environ[&#x27;CO_API_KEY&#x27;] or getpass(&quot;Enter your Cohere API key: &quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0058","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-009-3-1-using-llms","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s009","q":"How do you create a Cohere LLM and get one completion in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Create <code>Cohere</code> with a model and temperature, then call <code>complete</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from llama_index.llms.cohere import Cohere\n\nllm = Cohere(model=&quot;command-r-plus&quot;, temperature=0.2)\nresponse = llm.complete(&quot;Alexander the Great was a&quot;)   # single completion\nprint(response)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0059","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-009-3-1-using-llms","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s009","q":"How do you use a prompt template in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Write a template string with placeholders, call <code>format</code>, and pass the result to <code>complete</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>template = &quot;&quot;&quot;Write a song about {thing} in the style of {style}.&quot;&quot;&quot;\nprompt = template.format(thing=&quot;a broken xylophone&quot;, style=&quot;parody rap&quot;)\nresponse = llm.complete(prompt)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0060","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-009-3-1-using-llms","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s009","q":"How do you send chat messages with roles to a LlamaIndex LLM?","a":"<p>Build <code>ChatMessage</code> objects with a role and content, then call <code>chat</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>messages = [\n    ChatMessage(role=&quot;system&quot;, content=&quot;You&#x27;re a hella punk bot from South Sacramento&quot;),\n    ChatMessage(role=&quot;user&quot;, content=&quot;Hey, what&#x27;s up dude.&quot;),\n]\nresponse = llm.chat(messages)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0061","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-009-3-1-using-llms","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s009","q":"How do you build a chat prompt template in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Make a list of <code>ChatMessage</code> objects with <code>MessageRole</code>, use a <code>{question}</code> placeholder, and wrap them in <code>ChatPromptTemplate</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>chat_template = [\n    ChatMessage(role=MessageRole.SYSTEM, content=&quot;You always answers questions with as much detail as possible.&quot;),\n    ChatMessage(role=MessageRole.USER, content=&quot;{question}&quot;)\n]\nchat_prompt = ChatPromptTemplate(chat_template)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0062","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-009-3-1-using-llms","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s009","q":"How do you fill a chat prompt template and call the LLM?","a":"<p>Call <code>format</code> on the template and pass the result to <code>complete</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>response = llm.complete(chat_prompt.format(question=&quot;How far did Alexander the Great go in his conquests?&quot;))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0063","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-009-3-1-using-llms","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s009","q":"How do you stream a chat response in LlamaIndex, and why?","a":"<p>Streaming gives a better UX. Call <code>stream_chat</code> and print each <code>delta</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>response = llm.stream_chat(messages)\nfor r in response:\n    print(r.delta, end=&quot;&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0064","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-009-3-1-using-llms","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s009","q":"How do you create a simple chat engine with no retrieval and an interactive REPL?","a":"<p>Use <code>SimpleChatEngine.from_defaults</code> and call <code>chat_repl</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from llama_index.core.chat_engine import SimpleChatEngine\n\nchat_engine = SimpleChatEngine.from_defaults(llm=llm)\nchat_engine.chat_repl()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0065","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-009-3-1-using-llms","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s009","q":"What do <code>llm.complete</code>, <code>llm.chat</code>, <code>llm.stream_chat</code> and the chat engine methods do?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>llm.complete(prompt)</code></td><td>Single text completion</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>llm.chat(messages)</code></td><td>Chat with message history</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>llm.stream_chat(messages)</code></td><td>Streaming chat</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>chat_engine.chat(msg)</code> / <code>.chat_repl()</code> / <code>.streaming_chat_repl()</code></td><td>Conversational interface / REPL / streaming REPL</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0066","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-009-3-1-using-llms","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s009","q":"How can you list the available methods of any LlamaIndex object?","a":"<p>Use <code>dir(obj)</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0067","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-010-3-2-loading-data","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s010","q":"What are the three stages of ingestion in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p><strong>Load</strong> (Reader to Documents), <strong>Transform</strong> (Documents to Nodes: chunking, metadata, embeddings), and <strong>Index &amp; store</strong> (vector DB). It resembles ETL or ML data cleaning.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0068","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-010-3-2-loading-data","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s010","q":"What is a Reader, and what does a <code>Document</code> contain?","a":"<p>A Reader (data connector) formats data into <code>Document</code> objects. A <code>Document</code> holds text, metadata, an id and an embedding slot.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0069","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-010-3-2-loading-data","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s010","q":"Which file types does <code>SimpleDirectoryReader</code> read, and how are PDFs split?","a":"<p>It reads markdown, PDF, Word, PowerPoint, images, audio and video. PDFs give one Document per page.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0070","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-010-3-2-loading-data","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s010","q":"How do you load a whole directory or specific files with <code>SimpleDirectoryReader</code>?","a":"<p>Pass the directory path, or <code>input_files</code> with a list of files.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>documents = SimpleDirectoryReader(&quot;./data&quot;).load_data()          # whole directory\ndocuments = SimpleDirectoryReader(input_files=[&quot;./data/naval_almanack.pdf&quot;]).load_data()  # specific files</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0071","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-010-3-2-loading-data","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s010","q":"How do you check what type a loaded document is and which fields it has?","a":"<p>Print its type and the keys of its <code>__dict__</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>print(type(documents[0]))            # llama_index.core.schema.Document\nprint(documents[0].__dict__.keys())  # id_, embedding, metadata, text, ...</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0072","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-010-3-2-loading-data","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s010","q":"How do you create a <code>Document</code> manually, with metadata at creation or afterwards?","a":"<p>Pass <code>text</code> and optionally <code>metadata</code>, or set <code>doc.metadata</code> later.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>doc = Document(text=&quot;This is an example of a manual document&quot;)\ndoc = Document(\n    text=&quot;This is an example of a manual document&quot;,\n    metadata={&quot;filename&quot;: &quot;made-up-file-name&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;imaginary-category&quot;}\n)\ndoc.metadata = {&quot;filename&quot;: &quot;made-up-file-name&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;imaginary-category&quot;}  # or set later</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0073","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-010-3-2-loading-data","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s010","q":"How does the notebook download Project Gutenberg books 1 to 10?","a":"<p>It formats a URL per book id, downloads each one, and saves the text as <code>pg&lt;id&gt;.txt</code> in <code>../data</code>, printing an error on a bad status code.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>base_url = &quot;https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/{book_id}/pg{book_id}.txt&quot;\ndirectory = Path(&quot;../data&quot;)\ndirectory.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nurls = [base_url.format(book_id=book_id) for book_id in range(1, 11)]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0074","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-010-3-2-loading-data","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s010","q":"What is a node in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>A chunk of a document and the first-class citizen in LlamaIndex (<code>Document</code> is a subclass of <code>Node</code>). A node holds text, metadata, relationships to other nodes, and a link to its source document.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0075","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-010-3-2-loading-data","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s010","q":"What is a node parser?","a":"<p>A component that turns documents into nodes.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0076","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-010-3-2-loading-data","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s010","q":"How do you split documents into nodes with <code>SentenceSplitter</code>?","a":"<p>Create the splitter with a chunk size and overlap in tokens and a paragraph separator, then call <code>get_nodes_from_documents</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>parser = SentenceSplitter(\n    chunk_size=128,       # tokens\n    chunk_overlap=16,     # tokens\n    paragraph_separator=&quot;\\n\\n&quot;\n)\nnodes = parser.get_nodes_from_documents(documents, show_progress=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0077","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-010-3-2-loading-data","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s010","q":"What type are the nodes from <code>SentenceSplitter</code>, and what fields do they have?","a":"<p>They are <code>TextNode</code> objects with <code>id_</code>, <code>text</code>, <code>metadata</code> (page_label, file_name, ...) and <code>relationships</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>print(type(nodes[42]))              # TextNode</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0078","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-010-3-2-loading-data","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s010","q":"What are node relationships, and when are they useful?","a":"<p>They link chunks sequentially (NEXT and PREVIOUS) or hierarchically (PARENT and CHILD). They are useful for books with chapters and legal docs with clauses.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0079","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-010-3-2-loading-data","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s010","q":"How do you create two <code>TextNode</code> objects and link them with NEXT and PREVIOUS?","a":"<p>Set <code>relationships</code> on each node with <code>RelatedNodeInfo</code> pointing to the other node id.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>node1 = TextNode(text=&quot;Dad is married to Mom&quot;, id_=&quot;001&quot;)\nnode2 = TextNode(text=&quot;Dad is Son&#x27;s dad&quot;, id_=&quot;002&quot;)\n\nnode1.relationships[NodeRelationship.NEXT] = RelatedNodeInfo(node_id=node2.node_id)\nnode2.relationships[NodeRelationship.PREVIOUS] = RelatedNodeInfo(node_id=node1.node_id)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0080","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-010-3-2-loading-data","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s010","q":"How do you add a PARENT relationship with metadata to a node?","a":"<p>Use <code>NodeRelationship.PARENT</code> with <code>RelatedNodeInfo</code>, and pass a <code>metadata</code> dict.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>node2.relationships[NodeRelationship.PARENT] = RelatedNodeInfo(\n    node_id=node1.node_id,\n    metadata={&quot;Romie&quot;: &quot;Mom&quot;, &quot;Harpreet&quot;: &quot;Dad&quot;, &quot;Jind&quot;: &quot;Daughter&quot;, &quot;Jugaad&quot;: &quot;Son&quot;},\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0081","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-011-3-3-indexing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s011","q":"What is an index in LlamaIndex, and what is built from it?","a":"<p>A data structure for fast retrieval of relevant context for a query. Indexes build Retrievers, Query Engines and Chat Engines.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0082","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-011-3-3-indexing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s011","q":"What is the indexing flow in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Raw text, then Document, then Nodes, then embeddings, then the vector DB.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0083","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-011-3-3-indexing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s011","q":"What is an embedding, and what decides its length?","a":"<p>A fixed-length numeric vector representing the meaning of a text. The length depends on the model, never on the input length.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0084","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-011-3-3-indexing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s011","q":"What are the embedding dimensions of Cohere and OpenAI models used in the course?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Dimensions</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Cohere embed-english-v3.0</td><td>1024</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Cohere embed-english-light-v3.0</td><td>384</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Cohere embed-english-v2.0</td><td>4096</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>OpenAI text-embedding-3-small</td><td>1536</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0085","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-011-3-3-indexing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s011","q":"How do you create Cohere embedding models in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Use <code>CohereEmbedding</code> with a <code>model_name</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>embed_v3 = CohereEmbedding(model_name=&quot;embed-english-v3.0&quot;)\nembed_v3_light = CohereEmbedding(model_name=&quot;embed-english-light-v3.0&quot;)\nembed_v2 = CohereEmbedding(model_name=&quot;embed-english-v2.0&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0086","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-011-3-3-indexing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s011","q":"How do you get the embedding of a text and check its length?","a":"<p>Call <code>get_text_embedding</code>, then take the <code>len</code> of the result.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>example_embedding = embed_v3.get_text_embedding(&quot;A&quot;)\nlen(example_embedding)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0087","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-011-3-3-indexing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s011","q":"How do you check embedding dimensions for many strings at once?","a":"<p>Use <code>get_text_embedding_batch</code> and take the length of each embedding. The length is the same for a 1-char string, a sentence and a long paragraph.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def get_embedding_dimensions(embed_model, list_of_strings):\n    embeddings = embed_model.get_text_embedding_batch(list_of_strings)\n    return [len(embedding) for embedding in embeddings]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0088","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-011-3-3-indexing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s011","q":"How do you compute the cosine similarity between two embeddings in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Call <code>similarity</code> on the embedding model with <code>mode=\"cosine\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>embed_v3.similarity(\n    embed_v3.get_text_embedding(&quot;In embracing both the wisdom of the Sikh Gurus and the Stoic philosophers, ...&quot;),\n    embed_v3.get_text_embedding(string_2),\n    mode=&quot;cosine&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0089","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-011-3-3-indexing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s011","q":"Where do you compare local embedding models, and what are FastEmbed models?","a":"<p>Check the <strong>MTEB leaderboard</strong>. <strong>FastEmbed</strong> models are lightweight, quantized and CPU-optimized.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0090","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-011-3-3-indexing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s011","q":"How do you use a local Hugging Face embedding model in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Install <code>llama-index-embeddings-huggingface</code> and create <code>HuggingFaceEmbedding</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># pip install llama-index-embeddings-huggingface\nfrom llama_index.embeddings.huggingface import HuggingFaceEmbedding\nhf_embed_model = HuggingFaceEmbedding(model_name=&quot;BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0091","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-011-3-3-indexing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s011","q":"How do you use a FastEmbed model in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Install <code>llama-index-embeddings-fastembed</code> and create <code>FastEmbedEmbedding</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># pip install llama-index-embeddings-fastembed\nfrom llama_index.embeddings.fastembed import FastEmbedEmbedding\nembed_model = FastEmbedEmbedding(model_name=&quot;BAAI/bge-large-en-v1.5-quantized&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0092","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-012-3-3-indexing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s011","q":"What are the three ways to create a <code>VectorStoreIndex</code>, and when do you use each?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Use when</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>VectorStoreIndex.from_documents(docs)</code></td><td>You have documents to embed and store (computes embeddings)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>VectorStoreIndex.from_vector_store(store)</code></td><td>Embeddings already live in an external vector store such as Qdrant</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>VectorStoreIndex(nodes)</code></td><td>You parsed nodes yourself (more control)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0093","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-012-3-3-indexing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s011","q":"Why does the indexing notebook index only a 10,000-character slice of one book?","a":"<p>Embedding calls cost time and money.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>partial_document = Document(text=text_content[50000:60000])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0094","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-012-3-3-indexing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s011","q":"How do you build a <code>VectorStoreIndex</code> from documents, and what must you pass?","a":"<p>Call <code>from_documents</code> with a list of documents.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>index = VectorStoreIndex.from_documents(\n    [partial_document], embed_model=embed_v3, show_progress=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0095","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-012-3-3-indexing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s011","q":"How do you build a <code>VectorStoreIndex</code> from nodes you parsed yourself?","a":"<p>Split the document with a <code>SentenceSplitter</code>, then pass the nodes to <code>VectorStoreIndex</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>splitter = SentenceSplitter(chunk_size=512, chunk_overlap=16, paragraph_separator=&quot;\\n\\n\\n\\n&quot;)\nnodes = splitter.get_nodes_from_documents([partial_document])\nindex_from_nodes = VectorStoreIndex(nodes, embed_model=embed_v3, show_progress=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0096","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-012-3-3-indexing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s011","q":"What does the <code>load_text_from_url(url)</code> helper do, and which text does it load?","a":"<p>It calls <code>requests.get</code>, then <code>raise_for_status()</code>, and returns <code>response.text</code> (or an error string on <code>RequestException</code>). It points at <code>https://www.gutenberg.org/files/10763/10763.txt</code>, <em>It Can Be Done</em>, a poetry book reused in later notebooks.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0097","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-013-3-4-storing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s012","q":"Where does an index live by default, and how can you persist it?","a":"<p>In memory. Re-indexing costs time and money, so persist it. The simplest option is <code>index.persist()</code> to disk. The course uses a vector database (<strong>Qdrant</strong>).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0098","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-013-3-4-storing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s012","q":"What are the steps to store an index in Qdrant?","a":"<p>Initialize the Qdrant client, create a vector store bound to a collection, assign it to a <code>StorageContext</code>, and build the index from that context.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0099","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-013-3-4-storing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s012","q":"How do you create a Qdrant vector store bound to a collection?","a":"<p>Create a <code>QdrantClient</code>, then a <code>QdrantVectorStore</code> with the client, a collection name and the embed model.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>client = qdrant_client.QdrantClient(url=QDRANT_URL, api_key=QDRANT_API_KEY)\nvector_store = QdrantVectorStore(\n    client=client,\n    collection_name=&quot;it_can_be_done&quot;,\n    embed_model=embed_model,\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0100","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-013-3-4-storing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s012","q":"How do you load a text file with stable document ids and split it into chunks?","a":"<p>Use <code>filename_as_id=True</code> in <code>SimpleDirectoryReader</code>, and a <code>SentenceSplitter</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>document = SimpleDirectoryReader(input_files=[&quot;data/pg10763.txt&quot;], filename_as_id=True).load_data()\nsentence_splitter = SentenceSplitter(chunk_size=512, chunk_overlap=16, paragraph_separator=&quot;\\n\\n\\n\\n&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0101","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-013-3-4-storing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s012","q":"How do you assign a Qdrant vector store to a storage context and build an index?","a":"<p>Create the context with <code>StorageContext.from_defaults</code>, then pass it to <code>from_documents</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>storage_context = StorageContext.from_defaults(vector_store=vector_store)\n\nindex = VectorStoreIndex.from_documents(\n    document,\n    show_progress=True,\n    store_nodes_override=True,\n    transformation=[sentence_splitter],\n    embed_model=embed_model,\n    storage_context=storage_context,\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0102","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-013-3-4-storing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s012","q":"What does <code>StorageContext</code> tell LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Where to put each kind of data:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><code>vector_store</code>: embeddings.</li>\n  <li><code>docstore</code>: nodes and documents.</li>\n  <li><code>index_store</code>: index metadata.</li>\n  <li><code>graph_store</code>: knowledge graphs.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0103","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-013-3-4-storing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s012","q":"What does the Qdrant dashboard show for a collection?","a":"<p>The collection, the vector dimension (1536 here), a visualization tab, and \"Find Similar\".</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0104","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-013-3-4-storing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s012","q":"Which embedding model and dimension does the storing example use?","a":"<p><code>text-embedding-3-small</code> from OpenAI, with 1536 dimensions.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>embed_model = OpenAIEmbedding(model_name=&quot;text-embedding-3-small&quot;)   # 1536 dims</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0105","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-014-3-5-retrieving","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s013","q":"What is a retriever in LlamaIndex, and how does it work?","a":"<p>The interface an index exposes to fetch relevant nodes. The query is embedded with the same model used at indexing, a similarity search runs, and the <strong>top-k</strong> nodes come back with scores.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0106","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-014-3-5-retrieving","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s013","q":"Which retriever types does LlamaIndex have?","a":"<p>Vector, fusion, and recursive (hierarchical via node relationships).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0107","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-014-3-5-retrieving","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s013","q":"How do you create a retriever with top-k and a similarity threshold?","a":"<p>Call <code>as_retriever</code> on the index with <code>similarity_top_k</code> and <code>similarity_threshold</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>retriever = index.as_retriever(\n    similarity_top_k=5,\n    similarity_threshold=0.75)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0108","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-014-3-5-retrieving","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s013","q":"How do you retrieve nodes for a query and print score, id and text?","a":"<p>Call <code>retrieve</code> and loop over the nodes.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>retrieved_nodes = retriever.retrieve(&quot;What lessons can be learned from the poems about success?&quot;)\nfor node in retrieved_nodes:\n    print(f&quot;Score: {node.score:.4f} | ID: {node.node_id} | Text: {node.text[:100]}...&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0109","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-014-3-5-retrieving","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s013","q":"Why close the Qdrant client after retrieving from a local index?","a":"<p>So you are not locked out of the local index.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>client.close()   # close so you&#x27;re not locked out of the (local) index</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0110","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-014-3-5-retrieving","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s013","q":"What is the difference between <code>similarity_cutoff</code> and <code>similarity_threshold</code> in <code>as_retriever</code>?","a":"<p>The lesson passes <code>similarity_cutoff=0.75</code> while the notebook uses <code>similarity_threshold=0.75</code>. For a reliable cutoff, use a <code>SimilarityPostprocessor(similarity_cutoff=...)</code> on a query engine.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0111","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-014-3-5-retrieving","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s013","q":"Why do you need a query engine when a retriever already exists?","a":"<p>Retrieval returns raw nodes and scores. A query engine is needed for a synthesized answer.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0112","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-015-3-6-querying","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s014","q":"What is querying in LlamaIndex, and what are its stages?","a":"<p>A prompt call to the LLM with retrieved context. The stages are <strong>Retrieval</strong> (top-k), <strong>Postprocessing</strong> (rerank, filter or transform nodes) and <strong>Response synthesis</strong> (query + context + prompt to the LLM).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0113","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-015-3-6-querying","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s014","q":"How do you reconnect to an existing Qdrant collection without re-embedding?","a":"<p>Use <code>VectorStoreIndex.from_vector_store</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>index = VectorStoreIndex.from_vector_store(\n    vector_store=vector_store,\n    embed_model=embed_model,\n    storage_context=storage_context\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0114","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-015-3-6-querying","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s014","q":"How do you create a streaming query engine and print the streamed answer?","a":"<p>Pass <code>streaming=True</code> to <code>as_query_engine</code>, query, then print the stream.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query_engine = index.as_query_engine(llm=llm, streaming=True)\nresponse = query_engine.query(&quot;What do the Sikh Stoics believe?&quot;)\nresponse.print_response_stream()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0115","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-015-3-6-querying","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s014","q":"How do you see which nodes support a query-engine answer?","a":"<p>Read <code>response.source_nodes</code>, and call <code>get_text()</code> on a node.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>response.source_nodes                    # retrieved nodes behind the answer\nresponse.source_nodes[0].get_text()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0116","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-015-3-6-querying","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s014","q":"What is a chat engine?","a":"<p>Multi-turn querying with memory.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0117","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-015-3-6-querying","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s014","q":"What do the <code>simple</code> and <code>condense_question</code> chat modes do?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>simple</code>: plain LLM chat with no knowledge base (<code>SimpleChatEngine</code>).</li>\n  <li><code>condense_question</code>: rewrites history and the last message into a standalone question, then queries the engine (<code>CondenseQuestionChatEngine</code>).</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0118","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-015-3-6-querying","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s014","q":"What do the <code>context</code> and <code>condense_plus_context</code> chat modes do?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>context</code>: retrieves text for each user message and uses it as context (<code>ContextChatEngine</code>).</li>\n  <li><code>condense_plus_context</code>: condenses to a standalone question, retrieves context for it, then answers (<code>CondensePlusContextChatEngine</code>).</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0119","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-015-3-6-querying","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s014","q":"What do the <code>react</code> and <code>best</code> chat modes do?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>react</code>: a ReAct agent loop with query-engine tools.</li>\n  <li><code>best</code>: picks the best engine for the LLM, which is <code>OpenAIAgent</code> if function calling is supported, otherwise <code>ReActAgent</code>.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0120","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-016-3-6-querying","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s014","q":"How do you start a streaming chat REPL over an index?","a":"<p>Create a chat engine with <code>as_chat_engine</code> and call <code>streaming_chat_repl</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>chat_engine = index.as_chat_engine(llm=llm)\nchat_engine.streaming_chat_repl()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0121","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-016-3-6-querying","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s014","q":"How do you give a LlamaIndex chat engine a memory limit and a system prompt?","a":"<p>Create a <code>ChatMemoryBuffer</code> with a token limit, then pass <code>memory</code>, <code>chat_mode=\"context\"</code> and <code>system_prompt</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>memory = ChatMemoryBuffer.from_defaults(token_limit=1500)\nchat_engine = index.as_chat_engine(\n    llm=llm,\n    chat_mode=&quot;context&quot;,\n    memory=memory,\n    system_prompt=(\n        &quot;You are a chatbot, able to have normal interactions, as well as talk&quot;\n        &quot; about a book of poems called &#x27;It Can Be Done&#x27;.&quot;\n    ),\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0122","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-016-3-6-querying","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s014","q":"What can you control when customizing the query pipeline at a low level?","a":"<p>The retrieval <code>top_k</code>, the postprocessors (for example a minimum similarity), and the response synthesizer.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0123","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-016-3-6-querying","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s014","q":"How do you build the parts of a custom query engine with top-k 10 and a 0.42 similarity cutoff?","a":"<p>Create a <code>VectorIndexRetriever</code>, a <code>SimilarityPostprocessor</code> and a response synthesizer.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>retriever = VectorIndexRetriever(index=index, similarity_top_k=10)\nsimilarity_processor = SimilarityPostprocessor(similarity_cutoff=0.42)\nresponse_synthsizer = get_response_synthesizer(llm=llm)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0124","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-016-3-6-querying","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s014","q":"How do you assemble a <code>RetrieverQueryEngine</code> from a retriever, a synthesizer and postprocessors?","a":"<p>Pass them to the constructor.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query_engine = RetrieverQueryEngine(\n    retriever=retriever,\n    response_synthesizer=response_synthsizer,\n    node_postprocessors=[similarity_processor],\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0125","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-016-3-6-querying","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s014","q":"Query engine vs chat engine in LlamaIndex?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Query engine</th><th>Chat engine</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Interaction</td><td>Single question to answer</td><td>Multi-turn</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Memory</td><td>None</td><td>Keeps history</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Created by</td><td><code>index.as_query_engine()</code></td><td><code>index.as_chat_engine()</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0126","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-017-3-7-agents","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s015","q":"What is an agent in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>An LLM-powered entity that decomposes complex queries, selects tools and parameters, plans and executes. Agentic behavior is essentially a sophisticated prompting strategy plus tool access.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0127","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-017-3-7-agents","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s015","q":"What is ReAct?","a":"<p>Reasoning + Acting. The agent reasons step by step and decides when to call tools.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0128","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-017-3-7-agents","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s015","q":"Why do tool docstrings matter for an agent?","a":"<p>The agent reads the docstring and the type signature to decide when and how to call the tool.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0129","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-017-3-7-agents","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s015","q":"Why does the agent demo use \"alternate universe\" math tools?","a":"<p>So the answer cannot come from the LLM's memory.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0130","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-017-3-7-agents","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s015","q":"How do you turn a Python function into a LlamaIndex tool?","a":"<p>Use <code>FunctionTool.from_defaults</code> with the function and a name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>multiply_tool = FunctionTool.from_defaults(fn=multiply, name=&quot;multiply&quot;)\nadd_tool = FunctionTool.from_defaults(fn=add, name=&quot;add&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0131","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-017-3-7-agents","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s015","q":"How do you see the name and description a LlamaIndex tool derives from its docstring?","a":"<p>Print the tool metadata <code>__dict__</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>multiply_tool.metadata.__dict__          # name/description derived from the docstring</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0132","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-017-3-7-agents","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s015","q":"How do you create a ReAct agent with tools, and how do you see its reasoning?","a":"<p>Use <code>ReActAgent.from_tools</code> with the tools and the LLM. <code>verbose=True</code> shows the reasoning.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>llm = Cohere(model=&quot;command-r&quot;)\nagent = ReActAgent.from_tools([multiply_tool, add_tool], llm=llm, verbose=True)   # verbose shows reasoning</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0133","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-017-3-7-agents","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s015","q":"How do you inspect the ReAct system prompt of an agent?","a":"<p>Read the <code>agent_worker:system_prompt</code> entry of <code>get_prompts()</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>print(agent.get_prompts()[&#x27;agent_worker:system_prompt&#x27;].template)   # inspect the ReAct prompt</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0134","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-017-3-7-agents","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s015","q":"How do you check the agent's answer against ground truth in the demo?","a":"<p>Compute the expression by hand with the same functions, then call <code>agent.chat</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>add(multiply(3, 4), 5)    # ground truth to compare against\nresponse = agent.chat(&quot;You live in an alternate universe. Math works according to the tools provided. Use the provided tools to multiply 3 by 4 and add 5 to the result&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0135","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-017-3-7-agents","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s015","q":"What did the agent demo show about different LLMs?","a":"<p>Different LLMs differ in tool use. Command-R beat Command-R+ in the demo, so test multiple models.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0136","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-018-4-1-components-and-subsystems","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s016","q":"What is RAG in terms of its components?","a":"<p>Retrieve context from external data, add it to the prompt, then generate with the LLM.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0137","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-018-4-1-components-and-subsystems","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s016","q":"What is the role of each RAG component?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>LLM</td><td>Generates the answer from the augmented prompt</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Prompt / user input</td><td>The query that starts the pipeline; template that combines query + context</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Document loader</td><td>Reads raw data into Documents</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Chunker (node parser)</td><td>Splits documents into manageable chunks</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Embedding model</td><td>Turns chunks and queries into vectors</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Vector store</td><td>Stores and indexes embeddings</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Retriever</td><td>Fetches relevant chunks by vector similarity</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0138","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-018-4-1-components-and-subsystems","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s016","q":"What are the three RAG subsystems and their steps?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Subsystem</th><th>Steps</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Indexing</strong></td><td>Load, chunk, embed, store embeddings</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Retrieval</strong></td><td>Embed the query (same embedding model), vector search, relevant chunks</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Augment &amp; generate</strong></td><td>Build prompt (query + context), LLM, response</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0139","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-018-4-1-components-and-subsystems","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s016","q":"Which embedding model must the query use in the retrieval subsystem?","a":"<p>The same embedding model that was used at indexing.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0140","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-019-4-2-ingestion-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s017","q":"What is the LlamaIndex ingestion pipeline?","a":"<p>A higher-level abstraction over the low-level load, parse and index APIs. It applies <strong>transformations</strong> (split, embed, extract metadata), and returns nodes or inserts them into a vector store.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0141","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-019-4-2-ingestion-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s017","q":"How does caching work in the ingestion pipeline?","a":"<p>Each (node, transformation) pair is hashed and cached, and identical later runs reuse results.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0142","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-019-4-2-ingestion-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s017","q":"How does document management work when a docstore is attached to the ingestion pipeline?","a":"<p>The docstore tracks <code>doc_id</code> to <code>document_hash</code>. Same id with a changed hash means reprocess. Same id with the same hash means skip.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0143","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-019-4-2-ingestion-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s017","q":"What can the ingestion pipeline docstore do without and with a vector store?","a":"<p>Without a vector store it can only detect and remove duplicate inputs. With a vector store it handles <strong>upserts</strong> of updated documents.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0144","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-019-4-2-ingestion-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s017","q":"How do you persist the ingestion pipeline, and where?","a":"<p>Call <code>pipeline.persist()</code>. It saves the cache and docstore (default <code>./pipeline_storage</code>), as <code>docstore.json</code> and <code>cache.json</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pipeline.persist(&#x27;./pipeline_storage&#x27;)    # writes docstore.json + cache.json</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0145","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-019-4-2-ingestion-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s017","q":"How do you set global defaults for the LLM and embedding model in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Assign <code>Settings.llm</code> and <code>Settings.embed_model</code>. Every LlamaIndex component uses them.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Settings.llm = Cohere(model=&quot;command-r-plus&quot;, api_key=CO_API_KEY)\nSettings.embed_model = OpenAIEmbedding(model_name=&quot;text-embedding-3-small&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0146","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-019-4-2-ingestion-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s017","q":"Why load documents with <code>filename_as_id=True</code> before an ingestion pipeline?","a":"<p>Stable doc ids enable duplicate detection.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>documents = SimpleDirectoryReader(\n    input_files=[&quot;../02_Fundamental_Concepts_in_LlamaIndex/data/pg10763.txt&quot;],\n    filename_as_id=True).load_data()          # stable doc ids enable duplicate detection</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0147","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-019-4-2-ingestion-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s017","q":"How do you create the Qdrant vector store and ingestion cache for an ingestion pipeline?","a":"<p>Create a <code>QdrantVectorStore</code> and an <code>IngestionCache</code> for the same collection.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>vector_store = QdrantVectorStore(client=client, collection_name=&quot;it_can_be_done&quot;)\ningest_cache = IngestionCache(collection=&quot;it_can_be_done&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0148","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-019-4-2-ingestion-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s017","q":"How do you define and run an <code>IngestionPipeline</code> with a splitter, an embedding step, a docstore, a vector store and a cache?","a":"<p>Pass the transformations, docstore, vector store and cache, then call <code>run</code>. The embedding model is a transformation too.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pipeline = IngestionPipeline(\n    transformations=[\n        TokenTextSplitter(chunk_size=256, chunk_overlap=16),\n        Settings.embed_model          # embedding is a transformation too\n    ],\n    docstore=SimpleDocumentStore(),\n    vector_store=vector_store,\n    cache=ingest_cache,\n)\nnodes = pipeline.run(documents=documents)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0149","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-019-4-2-ingestion-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s017","q":"How do you build an index over ingested data and retrieve from it?","a":"<p>Use <code>from_vector_store</code>, then <code>as_retriever</code> and <code>retrieve</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>index = VectorStoreIndex.from_vector_store(vector_store=vector_store)\nretrieved_nodes = retriever.retrieve(&quot;Poems about starting where you stand, and not making dreams your master&quot;)\nprint(retrieved_nodes[0].get_text())\nprint(retrieved_nodes[0].get_score())</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0150","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-019-4-2-ingestion-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s017","q":"Low-level API vs ingestion pipeline: pros and cons?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Low-level API</th><th>Ingestion pipeline</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Pros</td><td>Full control per step</td><td>Less boilerplate, caching, dedupe/upserts</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Cons</td><td>More code</td><td>Less granular control</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0151","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-020-4-3-query-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s018","q":"What is the LlamaIndex query pipeline?","a":"<p>A declarative API to chain LLMs, prompts, retrievers, rerankers and other pipelines, either as a <strong>sequential chain</strong> or a <strong>DAG</strong>. It needs fewer lines and reads better.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0152","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-020-4-3-query-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s018","q":"When do you use the chain pattern of the query pipeline?","a":"<p>When each module takes one input. The course demo wraps a retriever in two prompts.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0153","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-020-4-3-query-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s018","q":"How do you define the two prompt templates and the retriever of the chain example?","a":"<p>Use <code>PromptTemplate</code> for each prompt, and <code>as_retriever</code> for the retriever.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>prompt_tmpl1 = PromptTemplate(&quot;Retrieve context about the following topic: {topic}&quot;)\nretriever = index.as_retriever(similarity_top_k=5)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0154","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-020-4-3-query-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s018","q":"How do you build and run a query pipeline as a chain?","a":"<p>Pass <code>chain</code> with prompts, retriever and LLM to <code>QueryPipeline</code>, then call <code>run</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>p = QueryPipeline(\n    chain=[prompt_tmpl1, retriever, prompt_tmpl2, Settings.llm],\n    verbose=True\n)\nresponse = p.run(topic=&quot;Working hard to achieve your goals even when you doubt yourself and your chances of success&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0155","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-020-4-3-query-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s018","q":"How do you see the inputs and outputs of every step of a query pipeline?","a":"<p>Use <code>run_with_intermediates</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>output, intermediates = p.run_with_intermediates(topic=&quot;Working hard to achieve your goals ...&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0156","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-020-4-3-query-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s018","q":"When do you need explicit modules and links in a query pipeline?","a":"<p>When one input feeds several modules (use <code>InputComponent</code>), or for DAGs.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0157","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-020-4-3-query-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s018","q":"How do you create the modules of an explicit query pipeline?","a":"<p>Create an <code>InputComponent</code>, a retriever and a <code>TreeSummarize</code>, then register them with <code>add_modules</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>input = InputComponent()\ntree_summarizer = TreeSummarize(llm=llm)\n\np = QueryPipeline(verbose=True, show_progress=True)\np.add_modules({\n    &quot;input&quot;: input,\n    &quot;retriever&quot;: retriever,\n    &quot;tree_summarizer&quot;: tree_summarizer,\n})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0158","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-020-4-3-query-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s018","q":"How do you link modules in an explicit query pipeline?","a":"<p>Use <code>add_link</code>, with <code>dest_key</code> to name the target input.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>p.add_link(&quot;input&quot;, &quot;retriever&quot;)\np.add_link(&quot;input&quot;, &quot;tree_summarizer&quot;, dest_key=&quot;query_str&quot;)\np.add_link(&quot;retriever&quot;, &quot;tree_summarizer&quot;, dest_key=&quot;nodes&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0159","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-020-4-3-query-pipeline","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s018","q":"How do you run an explicit query pipeline?","a":"<p>Call <code>run</code> with the <code>input</code> argument.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>response = p.run(input=&quot;Working hard to achieve your goals even when you doubt yourself and your chances of success&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0160","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-021-4-4-helper-utilities-helpers-utils-py","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s019","q":"What is <code>helpers/utils.py</code> in the course?","a":"<p>Thin wrappers used by all later notebooks. Knowing what they do makes the later code readable.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0161","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-021-4-4-helper-utilities-helpers-utils-py","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s019","q":"What do <code>setup_llm</code> and <code>setup_embed_model</code> do?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>setup_llm(provider, model, api_key)</code> sets <code>Settings.llm</code> for <code>cohere</code>, <code>openai</code> or <code>mistral</code>.</li>\n  <li><code>setup_embed_model(provider, **kw)</code> sets <code>Settings.embed_model</code>: <code>cohere</code> (embed-english-v3.0), <code>openai</code> (text-embedding-3-large unless overridden), <code>fastembed</code> (BAAI/bge-base-en-v1.5).</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0162","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-021-4-4-helper-utilities-helpers-utils-py","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s019","q":"What does <code>setup_vector_store</code> do?","a":"<p><code>setup_vector_store(url, key, collection, enable_hybrid=False)</code> builds a <code>QdrantVectorStore</code> with both sync and async Qdrant clients.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0163","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-021-4-4-helper-utilities-helpers-utils-py","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s019","q":"What do <code>get_documents_from_docstore</code> and <code>create_index</code> do?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>get_documents_from_docstore(persist_dir)</code> loads a persisted <code>SimpleDocumentStore</code> and returns its documents.</li>\n  <li><code>create_index(from_where, **kw)</code>: <code>\"vector_store\"</code> calls <code>VectorStoreIndex.from_vector_store</code>, <code>\"docs\"</code> calls <code>from_documents</code>.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0164","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-021-4-4-helper-utilities-helpers-utils-py","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s019","q":"What do <code>ingest</code>, <code>create_query_pipeline</code> and <code>create_query_engine</code> do?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>ingest(transformations, documents, **kw)</code> runs an <code>IngestionPipeline</code> (<code>pipeline.run(nodes=documents)</code>).</li>\n  <li><code>create_query_pipeline(chain, verbose=True)</code> returns <code>QueryPipeline(chain=chain)</code>.</li>\n  <li><code>create_query_engine(index, mode, **kw)</code>: <code>\"chat\"</code> gives <code>as_chat_engine</code>, <code>\"query\"</code> gives <code>as_query_engine</code>, <code>\"retrieve\"</code> gives <code>as_retriever</code>.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0165","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-021-4-4-helper-utilities-helpers-utils-py","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s019","q":"What do <code>display_prompt_dict</code> and the evaluation helpers do?","a":"<p><code>display_prompt_dict(prompts)</code> pretty-prints prompt templates in a notebook. <code>group_documents_by_author</code>, <code>sample_documents</code> and <code>run_generations_on_eval_set</code> are evaluation helpers.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0166","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-021-4-4-helper-utilities-helpers-utils-py","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s019","q":"How does the <code>setup_llm</code> helper choose the LLM class?","a":"<p>It checks the provider name and sets <code>Settings.llm</code>, and raises an error for an unknown provider.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def setup_llm(provider, model, api_key, **kwargs):\n    if provider == &quot;cohere&quot;:\n        Settings.llm = Cohere(model=model, api_key=api_key, **kwargs)\n    elif provider == &quot;openai&quot;:\n        Settings.llm = OpenAI(model=model, api_key=api_key, **kwargs)\n    elif provider == &quot;mistral&quot;:\n        Settings.llm = MistralAI(model=model, api_key=api_key, **kwargs)\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(f&quot;Invalid provider: {provider}. Pick one of &#x27;cohere&#x27;, &#x27;openai&#x27;, or &#x27;mistral&#x27;.&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0167","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-021-4-4-helper-utilities-helpers-utils-py","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s019","q":"How does the <code>setup_vector_store</code> helper create its Qdrant clients?","a":"<p>It creates a sync and an async client and returns a <code>QdrantVectorStore</code> with both.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def setup_vector_store(qdrant_url, qdrant_api_key, collection_name, enable_hybrid=False):\n    client = QdrantClient(location=qdrant_url, api_key=qdrant_api_key)\n    aclient = AsyncQdrantClient(location=qdrant_url, api_key=qdrant_api_key)\n    return QdrantVectorStore(client=client, aclient=aclient,\n                             collection_name=collection_name, enable_hybrid=enable_hybrid)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0168","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-021-4-4-helper-utilities-helpers-utils-py","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s019","q":"How does <code>get_documents_from_docstore</code> load documents?","a":"<p>It loads the docstore from the persist directory and returns the list of its documents.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def get_documents_from_docstore(persist_dir):\n    docstore = SimpleDocumentStore.from_persist_dir(persist_dir=persist_dir)\n    return list(docstore.docs.values())</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0169","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-022-4-4-helper-utilities-helpers-utils-py","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s019","q":"How does the <code>ingest</code> helper run an ingestion pipeline?","a":"<p>It creates an <code>IngestionPipeline</code> with the transformations and extra arguments, then runs it on the documents.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def ingest(transformations, documents, **kwargs):\n    pipeline = IngestionPipeline(transformations=transformations, **kwargs)\n    return pipeline.run(nodes=documents)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0170","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-022-4-4-helper-utilities-helpers-utils-py","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s019","q":"How does <code>create_query_engine</code> map its mode to an object?","a":"<p><code>\"chat\"</code> gives a chat engine, <code>\"query\"</code> a query engine, <code>\"retrieve\"</code> a retriever, and anything else raises an error.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def create_query_engine(index, mode, **kwargs):\n    if mode == &quot;chat&quot;:\n        return index.as_chat_engine(**kwargs)\n    elif mode == &quot;query&quot;:\n        return index.as_query_engine(**kwargs)\n    elif mode == &quot;retrieve&quot;:\n        return index.as_retriever(**kwargs)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0171","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-022-4-4-helper-utilities-helpers-utils-py","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s019","q":"How does the <code>setup_embed_model</code> helper choose the embedding model?","a":"<p>It checks the provider and sets <code>Settings.embed_model</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def setup_embed_model(provider, **kwargs):\n    if provider == &quot;cohere&quot;:\n        Settings.embed_model = CohereEmbedding(model_name=&quot;embed-english-v3.0&quot;, **kwargs)\n    elif provider == &quot;openai&quot;:\n        Settings.embed_model = OpenAIEmbedding(model_name=&quot;text-embedding-3-large&quot;, **kwargs)\n    elif provider == &quot;fastembed&quot;:\n        Settings.embed_model = FastEmbedEmbedding(model_name=&quot;BAAI/bge-base-en-v1.5&quot;, **kwargs)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0172","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-022-4-4-helper-utilities-helpers-utils-py","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s019","q":"How does the <code>create_index</code> helper build an index?","a":"<p><code>\"vector_store\"</code> calls <code>from_vector_store</code>, <code>\"docs\"</code> calls <code>from_documents</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def create_index(from_where, embed_model=Settings.embed_model, **kwargs):\n    if from_where == &quot;vector_store&quot;:\n        return VectorStoreIndex.from_vector_store(embed_model=embed_model, **kwargs)\n    elif from_where == &quot;docs&quot;:\n        return VectorStoreIndex.from_documents(embed_model=embed_model, **kwargs)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0173","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-022-4-4-helper-utilities-helpers-utils-py","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s019","q":"How does the <code>create_query_pipeline</code> helper work?","a":"<p>It returns a <code>QueryPipeline</code> over the chain, verbose by default.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def create_query_pipeline(chain, verbose=True):\n    return QueryPipeline(chain=chain, verbose=verbose)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0174","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-022-4-4-helper-utilities-helpers-utils-py","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s019","q":"How does <code>display_prompt_dict</code> build its markdown?","a":"<p>It loops over the prompts dict, adds the key and the template text for each, and displays the markdown.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def display_prompt_dict(prompts_dict):\n    markdown_output = &quot; &quot;\n    for k, p in prompts_dict.items():\n        markdown_output += f&quot;**Prompt Key**: {k}\\n**Text:**\\n&quot; + p.get_template() + &quot;\\n\\n&quot;   # source wraps the text in a markdown code fence\n    display(Markdown(markdown_output))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0175","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-022-4-4-helper-utilities-helpers-utils-py","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s019","q":"How do you set up a typical course notebook with the helpers?","a":"<p>Add <code>../helpers</code> to the path, import the helpers, then set up the LLM and the embedding model.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>sys.path.append(&#x27;../helpers&#x27;)\nfrom utils import setup_llm, setup_embed_model, setup_vector_store, create_index\n\nsetup_llm(provider=&quot;cohere&quot;, model=&quot;command-r-plus&quot;, api_key=CO_API_KEY)\nsetup_embed_model(provider=&quot;openai&quot;, api_key=OPENAI_API_KEY)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0176","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-022-4-4-helper-utilities-helpers-utils-py","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s019","q":"How do you create the vector store, storage context and index with the helpers?","a":"<p>Call <code>setup_vector_store</code>, make a <code>StorageContext</code>, then <code>create_index</code> with <code>from_where=\"vector_store\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>COLLECTION_NAME = &quot;it_can_be_done&quot;\nvector_store = setup_vector_store(QDRANT_URL, QDRANT_API_KEY, COLLECTION_NAME)\nstorage_context = StorageContext.from_defaults(vector_store=vector_store)\nindex = create_index(from_where=&quot;vector_store&quot;, vector_store=vector_store, storage_context=storage_context)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0177","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-023-4-5-prompt-engineering-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s020","q":"How do you inspect and replace the prompt templates of a LlamaIndex query engine?","a":"<p>Inspect them with <code>get_prompts()</code> and replace one with <code>update_prompts()</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0178","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-023-4-5-prompt-engineering-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s020","q":"Which key controls the answer-generation prompt of a query engine, and which placeholders does it use?","a":"<p>The key <code>response_synthesizer:text_qa_template</code>, with placeholders <code>{context_str}</code> and <code>{query_str}</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0179","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-023-4-5-prompt-engineering-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s020","q":"How do you create a query engine and view its default prompts with the helpers?","a":"<p>Call <code>create_query_engine</code> with <code>mode=\"query\"</code>, then pass <code>query_engine.get_prompts()</code> to <code>display_prompt_dict</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>display_prompt_dict(query_engine.get_prompts())      # view default prompts</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0180","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-023-4-5-prompt-engineering-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s020","q":"What does the custom RAG prompt of the course ask the model to do?","a":"<p>It tells the assistant to answer questions about motivational poetry with an original Haiku style poem, using <code>{context_str}</code> and <code>{query_str}</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>custom_prompt_template = PromptTemplate(custom_prompt)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0181","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-023-4-5-prompt-engineering-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s020","q":"How do you replace the answer-generation prompt of a query engine?","a":"<p>Call <code>update_prompts</code> with the key <code>response_synthesizer:text_qa_template</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query_engine.update_prompts(\n    {&quot;response_synthesizer:text_qa_template&quot;: custom_prompt_template}\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0182","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-023-4-5-prompt-engineering-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s020","q":"How do you plug a query engine into a query pipeline?","a":"<p>Put an <code>InputComponent</code> and the engine in a chain, then run the pipeline with <code>input</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>input_component = InputComponent()\nchain = [input_component, query_engine]\nquery_pipeline = create_query_pipeline(chain)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0183","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-024-4-6-response-synthesizers-response-modes","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s021","q":"What do response synthesizers control, and how do you list the modes?","a":"<p>They control how retrieved chunks are combined and sent to the LLM. List the modes with <code>dir(ResponseMode)</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0184","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-024-4-6-response-synthesizers-response-modes","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s021","q":"What do the <code>refine</code> and <code>compact</code> response modes do?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>refine</code>: answers from node 1, then refines through nodes 2..N with one LLM call per node. It gives detailed answers with the most LLM calls.</li>\n  <li><code>compact</code>: packs chunks into larger ones that fill the context window, then refines. It makes fewer calls than refine.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0185","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-024-4-6-response-synthesizers-response-modes","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s021","q":"What do the <code>simple_summarize</code> and <code>tree_summarize</code> response modes do?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>simple_summarize</code>: merges all chunks into one call. It is fast, but fails if the merged text exceeds the context window and may truncate.</li>\n  <li><code>tree_summarize</code>: builds a summary tree bottom-up and returns the root. It is best for comprehensive multi-document summaries.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0186","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-024-4-6-response-synthesizers-response-modes","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s021","q":"What do the <code>generation</code> and <code>no_text</code> response modes do?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>generation</code>: ignores the context and uses the LLM only, for open-ended generation.</li>\n  <li><code>no_text</code>: retrieval only, so you can inspect <code>response.source_nodes</code>. It is for debugging retrieval.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0187","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-024-4-6-response-synthesizers-response-modes","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s021","q":"What do the <code>accumulate</code> and <code>compact_accumulate</code> response modes do?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>accumulate</code>: runs the query against each chunk and concatenates the answers (the same question per chunk).</li>\n  <li><code>compact_accumulate</code>: packs chunks first, then accumulates. It is faster than accumulate.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0188","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-024-4-6-response-synthesizers-response-modes","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s021","q":"How do you choose a response mode for a query engine?","a":"<p>Create the synthesizer with <code>get_response_synthesizer(response_mode=...)</code> and pass it to the engine.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>response_synthesizer = get_response_synthesizer(response_mode=&quot;compact&quot;)\nquery_engine = create_query_engine(index, mode=&quot;query&quot;, response_synthesizer=response_synthesizer)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0189","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-024-4-6-response-synthesizers-response-modes","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s021","q":"How do you run a query engine and the LLM as a chain in a query pipeline?","a":"<p>Put the input component, the query engine and <code>Settings.llm</code> in a chain.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>chain = [input_component, query_engine, Settings.llm]\nquery_pipeline = create_query_pipeline(chain)\nquery_pipeline.run(input=&quot;What do the poems teach about one should think about success and failure?&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0190","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-025-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"Why does data preparation matter for RAG?","a":"<p>A RAG system is only as good as the data it retrieves. Real PDFs have inconsistent layouts, images and charts (need OCR), tables, and header and footer noise. The course deliberately uses simple book PDFs.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0191","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-025-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"What should you consider when preparing documents for RAG?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Document <strong>content</strong>.</li>\n  <li>Document <strong>elements</strong>: title, narrative text, list items, tables, images.</li>\n  <li>Element <strong>metadata</strong>: filename, filetype, page number, section. It is used for filtering and hybrid search.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0192","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-025-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"What are the three PDF loaders the course compares?","a":"<p><code>SimpleDirectoryReader</code>, <code>SmartPDFLoader</code> (from <code>llama_index.readers.smart_pdf_loader</code>) and <code>PDFReader</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from llama_index.readers.file import PDFReader\nfrom llama_index.readers.smart_pdf_loader import SmartPDFLoader</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0193","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-025-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"How many documents does each PDF loader return for the Almanack, and why?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><code>SimpleDirectoryReader</code>: 242, one per page.</li>\n  <li><code>SmartPDFLoader</code>: 932, layout-aware chunks.</li>\n  <li><code>PDFReader</code>: 242, with the same text as <code>SimpleDirectoryReader</code>.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0194","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-025-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"How do you load a PDF with <code>SmartPDFLoader</code>?","a":"<p>Pass the LLMSherpa API URL, then call <code>load_data</code> with the path.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>smart_pdf_loader_docs = SmartPDFLoader(llmsherpa_api_url=LLMSHERPA_API_URL).load_data(PDF_PATH)  # 932, layout-aware chunks</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0195","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-025-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"How do you check that <code>PDFReader</code> and <code>SimpleDirectoryReader</code> give the same text?","a":"<p>Compare the text of the same page, which returns <code>True</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>pdf_reader_docs[100].text == simple_directory_reader_docs[100].text   # True</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0196","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-025-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"How do you extract the raw text of PDF pages with PyMuPDF?","a":"<p>Open the file with <code>fitz</code>, then call <code>get_text</code> with <code>sort=True</code> per page and split it into lines.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>document = fitz.open(PDF_PATH)\ndef extract_text(document, opt=&quot;text&quot;):\n    text = document.get_text(opt, sort=True)\n    text = text.split(&quot;\\n&quot;)\n    return text\npages = [extract_text(page) for page in document]    # first look at raw page text</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0197","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-025-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"What does the custom PyMuPDF extraction do for each book?","a":"<p>It selects page ranges per book, strips headers and footers, cleans the text, and attaches metadata.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0198","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-025-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"How does <code>get_document</code> keep only some pages of a PDF?","a":"<p>It opens the file and calls <code>select</code> with the page numbers when <code>pages</code> is not <code>None</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def get_document(file_path, pages):\n    document = fitz.open(file_path)\n    if pages is not None:\n        document.select(pages)\n    return document</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0199","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-026-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"What does <code>handle_chapter_headers_footers</code> do, and which flags does it accept?","a":"<p>It drops empty strings, then, if there are more than 3 lines, removes header and footer lines according to the flag: <code>remove_first</code>, <code>remove_last</code>, <code>remove_first_last</code> or <code>remove_first_two</code>. It returns the lines joined with spaces.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>return &#x27; &#x27;.join(filtered_strings).strip()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0200","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-026-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"How does <code>handle_chapter_headers_footers</code> apply each flag?","a":"<p>It slices the list of lines.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>if flag == &#x27;remove_first&#x27;:\n    filtered_strings = filtered_strings[1:]\nelif flag == &#x27;remove_last&#x27;:\n    filtered_strings = filtered_strings[:-1]\nelif flag == &#x27;remove_first_last&#x27;:\n    filtered_strings = filtered_strings[1:-1]\nelif flag == &#x27;remove_first_two&#x27;:\n    filtered_strings = filtered_strings[2:]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0201","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-026-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"Which metadata does <code>extract_text</code> attach to each page in the course extraction code?","a":"<p><code>page_number</code>, <code>file_name</code>, <code>title</code> and <code>author</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;metadata&quot;: {\n    &quot;page_number&quot;: page.number,\n    &quot;file_name&quot;: file_name,\n    &quot;title&quot;: title,\n    &quot;author&quot;: author\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0202","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-026-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"Which cleaning options does <code>extract_text</code> pass to <code>clean</code>?","a":"<p>Extra whitespace, broken paragraphs, bullets, ascii, citations and merge split words are on, and lowercase is off.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>text = clean(\n    text,\n    extra_whitespace=True,\n    broken_paragraphs=True,\n    bullets=True,\n    ascii=True,\n    lowercase=False,\n    citations=True,\n    merge_split_words=True,\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0203","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-026-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"How does <code>extract_texts_from_pdf</code> process a whole PDF?","a":"<p>It opens the file with the selected pages, then extracts and cleans each page.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def extract_texts_from_pdf(file_path, title, author, pages, flag):\n    document = get_document(file_path, pages)\n    return [extract_text(page, file_path, title, author, flag) for page in document]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0204","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-026-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"What is the useful point of the per-book <code>pdf_files</code> configuration?","a":"<p>Each book needs its own page range and header/footer rule.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0205","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-026-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"Which page range and flag does the Almanack of Naval Ravikant use?","a":"<p>Pages 29 to 202 with the flag <code>remove_last</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{&quot;file_path&quot;: &quot;../data/almanack_of_naval_ravikant.pdf&quot;, &quot;title&quot;: &quot;The Almanack of Naval Ravikant&quot;,\n &quot;author&quot;: &quot;Naval Ravikant&quot;, &quot;pages&quot;: list(range(29, 203)), &quot;flag&quot;: &quot;remove_last&quot;},</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0206","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-026-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"Which header/footer flags do the other books use?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Anthology of Balaji (pages 32 to 260): <code>remove_last</code>.</li>\n  <li>Hackers and Painters (pages 14 to 220): <code>remove_first_last</code>.</li>\n  <li>Skin in the Game (pages 15 to 271) and Striking Thoughts (pages 20 to 216): <code>None</code>.</li>\n  <li>Seneca volumes: <code>remove_first_two</code>.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0207","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-026-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"How do you loop over the book configs and collect all page texts?","a":"<p>Extract each PDF with its settings and extend one list.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>all_texts = []\nfor pdf in pdf_files:\n    texts = extract_texts_from_pdf(pdf[&quot;file_path&quot;], pdf[&quot;title&quot;], pdf[&quot;author&quot;], pdf[&quot;pages&quot;], pdf[&quot;flag&quot;])\n    all_texts.extend(texts)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0208","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-026-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"How do you wrap the cleaned pages in LlamaIndex <code>Document</code> objects?","a":"<p>Create a <code>Document</code> with the text and metadata of each page.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>llama_index_docs = [Document(text=doc[&quot;text&quot;], metadata=doc[&quot;metadata&quot;]) for doc in all_texts]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0209","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-026-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"Why persist a docstore after cleaning, and how?","a":"<p>So the cleaning runs once. Add the documents to a <code>SimpleDocumentStore</code>, put it in a <code>StorageContext</code>, and call <code>persist</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>docstore = SimpleDocumentStore()\ndocstore.add_documents(llama_index_docs)\nstorage_context = StorageContext.from_defaults(docstore=docstore)\nstorage_context.persist(&quot;../data/words-of-the-senpais&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0210","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-027-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"Where does <code>clean()</code> come from, and what are its options?","a":"<p>It lives in <code>helpers/text_cleaning_helpers.py</code>, adapted from the Unstructured library. Options: <code>extra_whitespace</code>, <code>broken_paragraphs</code>, <code>bullets</code> (strip unicode bullets), <code>ascii</code> (drop non-ASCII), <code>lowercase</code>, <code>citations</code> (remove <code>[1]</code>-style), <code>merge_split_words</code> (fix \"import- ant\" to \"important\").</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0211","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-027-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"What is the gotcha with <code>broken_paragraphs</code> in <code>clean()</code>?","a":"<p>In the provided source, <code>clean()</code> accepts <code>broken_paragraphs</code> but never applies it.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0212","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-027-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"What is the order of operations in <code>clean()</code>?","a":"<p>Lowercase, ascii, citations, extra_whitespace, bullets, merge_split_words.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># clean() order: lowercase -&gt; ascii -&gt; citations -&gt; extra_whitespace -&gt; bullets -&gt; merge_split_words</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0213","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-027-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"How do you drop non-ASCII characters from a string?","a":"<p>Encode to ascii while ignoring errors, then decode.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>en = text.encode(&quot;ascii&quot;, &quot;ignore&quot;)\nreturn en.decode()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0214","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-027-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"How does <code>clean_bullets</code> remove a leading unicode bullet?","a":"<p>It matches <code>UNICODE_BULLETS_RE</code> at the start of the text. If there is no match it returns the text. Otherwise it substitutes the bullet once with a space and strips the result. The regex covers ●, •, ‣, ◦, * and -.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>search = UNICODE_BULLETS_RE.match(text)\nif search is None:\n    return text\ncleaned_text = UNICODE_BULLETS_RE.sub(&quot; &quot;, text, 1)\nreturn cleaned_text.strip()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0215","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-027-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"How does <code>clean_extra_whitespace</code> work?","a":"<p>It replaces non-breaking spaces and newlines with spaces, collapses runs of two or more spaces, and strips the result (\"ITEM 1.     BUSINESS\" becomes \"ITEM 1. BUSINESS\").</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>cleaned_text = re.sub(r&quot;[\\xa0\\n]&quot;, &quot; &quot;, text)\ncleaned_text = re.sub(r&quot;([ ]{2,})&quot;, &quot; &quot;, cleaned_text)\nreturn cleaned_text.strip()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0216","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-027-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"How do you merge words split by a hyphen and a space?","a":"<p>Use a regex that joins the two word parts.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def merge_hyphenated_words(text):\n    pattern = r&#x27;(\\w+)-\\s+(\\w+)&#x27;\n    return re.sub(pattern, r&#x27;\\1\\2&#x27;, text)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0217","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-027-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"How do you remove <code>[1]</code>-style citations?","a":"<p>Use a lambda with a regex for one to three digits in brackets.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>remove_citations = lambda text: re.sub(r&quot;\\[\\d{1,3}\\]&quot;, &quot;&quot;, text)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0218","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-027-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"What does <code>group_broken_paragraphs</code> do, and is it used?","a":"<p>It is a regex-based paragraph re-joining function copied from Unstructured. It is not wired into <code>clean</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0219","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-027-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"Which tools help with general harder PDFs?","a":"<p>LlamaParse (paid, by LlamaIndex), pdfminer.six, pdfplumber (characters, lines, tables), pypdf, PyMuPDF, Camelot (tables), LLMSherpa (<code>LayoutPDFReader</code>), Unstructured, Table Transformer, Layout Parser, marker (PDF to markdown) and surya (OCR, layout).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0220","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-027-4-7-data-preparation-for-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s022","q":"Which tools help with academic PDFs?","a":"<p>nougat (LaTeX math and tables), GROBID (XML/TEI) and LaTeX-OCR.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0221","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-028-4-8-putting-it-together-naive-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s023","q":"What does \"naive\" mean in Naive RAG?","a":"<p>Default settings with no optimization.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0222","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-028-4-8-putting-it-together-naive-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s023","q":"What is the flow of the Naive RAG pipeline in the course?","a":"<p>Load persisted docs, chunk with <code>SentenceSplitter</code> (default <code>DEFAULT_CHUNK_SIZE</code> = 1024), embed, ingest into Qdrant, build an index over the vector store, create a query engine, then a query pipeline.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0223","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-028-4-8-putting-it-together-naive-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s023","q":"How do you set up the LLM, embedding model and vector store for Naive RAG?","a":"<p>Call the helpers with a collection name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>COLLECTION_NAME = &quot;words-of-the-senpai-naive&quot;\n\nsetup_llm(provider=&quot;cohere&quot;, model=&quot;command-r-plus&quot;, api_key=CO_API_KEY)\nsetup_embed_model(provider=&quot;openai&quot;, model_name=&quot;text-embedding-3-large&quot;, api_key=OPENAI_API_KEY)\nvector_store = setup_vector_store(QDRANT_URL, QDRANT_API_KEY, COLLECTION_NAME)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0224","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-028-4-8-putting-it-together-naive-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s023","q":"How do you load the persisted documents for Naive RAG?","a":"<p>Call <code>get_documents_from_docstore</code> with the persist directory.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>documents = get_documents_from_docstore(&quot;../data/words-of-the-senpais&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0225","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-028-4-8-putting-it-together-naive-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s023","q":"How do you ingest documents into Qdrant in Naive RAG?","a":"<p>Run <code>ingest</code> with a <code>SentenceSplitter</code> and the embedding model as transformations.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tranforms = [SentenceSplitter(chunk_size=DEFAULT_CHUNK_SIZE), Settings.embed_model]\nnodes = ingest(documents=documents, transformations=tranforms, vector_store=vector_store)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0226","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-028-4-8-putting-it-together-naive-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s023","q":"How do you create the index and query engine in Naive RAG?","a":"<p>Build the index from the vector store, then create a query engine. The LLM resolves to <code>Settings.llm</code> when it is not passed.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>index = create_index(from_where=&quot;vector_store&quot;, embed_model=Settings.embed_model, vector_store=vector_store)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0227","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-028-4-8-putting-it-together-naive-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s023","q":"How do you run the Naive RAG query pipeline and look at the first retrieved node?","a":"<p>Build the chain, run it with <code>input</code>, and read <code>source_nodes</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>input_component = InputComponent()\nchain = [input_component, query_engine]\nquery_pipeline = create_query_pipeline(chain)\nprint(response_1)\nresponse_1.source_nodes[0].__dict__</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0228","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-028-4-8-putting-it-together-naive-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s023","q":"Which test queries does the Naive RAG notebook use?","a":"<p>The mental models for important life decisions, the essence of a life well-lived, the role of luck in outsized success, and the commonalities between Naval and Taleb on luck. It is the same call with a different <code>input</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0229","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-029-4-9-drawbacks-of-naive-rag-interview-fav","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s024","q":"What are the three steps of the Naive RAG workflow?","a":"<p><strong>Index</strong> (chunk and index raw data), <strong>retrieve</strong> (search with the query), and <strong>generate</strong> (query plus retrieved context).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0230","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-029-4-9-drawbacks-of-naive-rag-interview-fav","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s024","q":"What are the indexing problems of Naive RAG?","a":"<p>Incomplete or inaccurate extraction, suboptimal chunking, inefficient indexing and poor semantic representation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0231","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-029-4-9-drawbacks-of-naive-rag-interview-fav","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s024","q":"What are the retrieval problems of Naive RAG?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Low precision</strong>: retrieved chunks that don't match.</li>\n  <li><strong>Low recall</strong>: relevant chunks are missed.</li>\n  <li>Ineffective user queries.</li>\n  <li>Redundant or overlapping chunks.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0232","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-029-4-9-drawbacks-of-naive-rag-interview-fav","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s024","q":"What are the generation problems of Naive RAG?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Hallucination</strong> not grounded in the context.</li>\n  <li>Hard to judge the relevance of the retrieved context.</li>\n  <li>Over-reliance on context (echoing without synthesis).</li>\n  <li>Biased, inconsistent or irrelevant output.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0233","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-029-4-9-drawbacks-of-naive-rag-interview-fav","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s024","q":"What addresses the drawbacks of Naive RAG in the course?","a":"<p>Advanced and modular RAG.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0234","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-030-5-rag-evaluation","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s025","q":"Why evaluate a RAG system?","a":"<p>Evaluation gives numbers for accuracy and relevance. It lets you compare models, prompts, contexts and retrieval strategies, track quality over time, and find which part of the pipeline to fix.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0235","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-031-5-1-what-to-evaluate","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s026","q":"What are the two RAG components to evaluate, and what is the challenge of each?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Phases</th><th>Evaluation challenge</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Retrieval</strong></td><td>Indexing (organize documents) + searching (fetch by query)</td><td>Is the filtering effective? Is the retrieved data relevant and useful?</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Generation</strong></td><td>Query + retrieved context to answer</td><td>Does the LLM use the context well? Is the answer factual, relevant, coherent?</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0236","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-031-5-1-what-to-evaluate","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s026","q":"What are the two quality dimensions of RAG evaluation?","a":"<p><strong>Relevance</strong> (precise context, answers related to the query) and <strong>Faithfulness</strong> (the answer is consistent with the retrieved context, with no contradictions).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0237","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-031-5-1-what-to-evaluate","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s026","q":"What are the four ability dimensions of RAG evaluation?","a":"<ul>\n  <li><strong>Noise robustness</strong>: handles noisy contexts.</li>\n  <li><strong>Negative rejection</strong>: admits a lack of knowledge.</li>\n  <li><strong>Information integration</strong>: combines information from multiple documents.</li>\n  <li><strong>Counterfactual robustness</strong>: ignores misinformation.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0238","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-032-5-2-metrics","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s027","q":"What is faithfulness in RAG evaluation?","a":"<p>The answer stays true to the context. It is key for catching hallucinations.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0239","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-032-5-2-metrics","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s027","q":"What are answer relevance and context relevance?","a":"<p><strong>Answer relevance</strong>: the answer addresses the question and stays on topic. <strong>Context relevance</strong>: the retrieved context is accurate and targeted, without irrelevant text that wastes LLM capacity.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0240","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-032-5-2-metrics","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s027","q":"What is MRR?","a":"<p>Mean Reciprocal Rank: the reciprocal of the rank of the first correct result, averaged across queries.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0241","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-032-5-2-metrics","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s027","q":"Which RAG metrics use the LLM-as-a-Judge paradigm?","a":"<p>Faithfulness, context relevance and answer relevance.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0242","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-032-5-2-metrics","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s027","q":"What is LLM-as-a-Judge?","a":"<p>A strong LLM scores other LLM outputs to approximate human judgment.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0243","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-032-5-2-metrics","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s027","q":"What are the benefits and limits of LLM-as-a-Judge?","a":"<p>Benefits: scalable, cheap, fast iteration. Limits: <strong>position bias</strong>, <strong>verbosity bias</strong> (prefers longer outputs), and weak reasoning on topics like math. GPT-4 reaches over 80% agreement with human preferences.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0244","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-032-5-2-metrics","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s027","q":"What further reading does the course recommend on RAG evaluation?","a":"<p>ARAGOG (advanced RAG output grading, recommended), ARES, \"Evaluation of Retrieval-Augmented Generation: A Survey\", and the Hugging Face cookbooks on RAG evaluation and LLM-as-a-judge.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0245","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-033-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"What is the hard part of RAG evaluation?","a":"<p>A high-quality evaluation dataset, not the metrics.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0246","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-033-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"What are the steps of the pipeline for building a synthetic RAG evaluation set in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Sample documents per author, chunk them, have an LLM write a question per chunk, have the LLM answer from the chunk, have a critic LLM score the question's groundedness, filter, then publish.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0247","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-033-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"Why does the evaluation-set demo use OpenAI instead of Cohere?","a":"<p>Cohere's free tier is rate-limited. The dataset is published, so rerunning is optional.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0248","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-033-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"How do you get a balanced sample of documents per author for the evaluation set?","a":"<p>Group the documents by author, then sample a fixed number per author with a seed set for repeatability.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>random.seed(42)\ndocuments_by_author = group_documents_by_author(documents)\ndocs_for_eval_set = sample_documents(documents_by_author, num_samples=25)   # balanced sample per author</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0249","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-033-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"How do you count the sampled documents per author as a sanity check?","a":"<p>Use a <code>Counter</code> over the <code>author</code> metadata.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def count_documents_by_author(documents):\n    return Counter(doc.metadata[&#x27;author&#x27;] for doc in documents if &#x27;author&#x27; in doc.metadata)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0250","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-033-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"How do you chunk the sampled pages before generating evaluation questions?","a":"<p>Run them through <code>ingest</code> with a <code>TokenTextSplitter</code> of 256 tokens and 32 overlap.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>splitter = TokenTextSplitter(chunk_size=256, chunk_overlap=32)\ndocs_for_eval_set = ingest(documents=docs_for_eval_set, transformations=[splitter])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0251","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-033-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"What does <code>group_documents_by_author</code> do?","a":"<p>It builds a <code>defaultdict(list)</code> keyed by <code>doc.metadata['author']</code>. It warns and skips documents with no author.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def group_documents_by_author(documents):\n    documents_by_author = defaultdict(list)\n    for doc in documents:\n        author = doc.metadata.get(&#x27;author&#x27;, None)\n        if author:\n            documents_by_author[author].append(doc)\n        else:\n            print(&quot;Warning: A document without an author was encountered and skipped.&quot;)\n    return documents_by_author</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0252","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-034-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"What does <code>sample_documents</code> do?","a":"<p>It keeps only documents longer than 500 characters, then uses <code>random.sample</code> to pick <code>num_samples</code> per author. It warns if an author has too few valid documents.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def sample_documents(documents_by_author, num_samples=10):\n    sampled_documents = []\n    for author, docs in documents_by_author.items():\n        valid_docs = [doc for doc in docs if len(doc.get_content()) &gt; 500]\n        if len(valid_docs) &gt;= num_samples:\n            sampled_documents.extend(random.sample(valid_docs, num_samples))\n        else:\n            print(f&quot;Author {author} does not have enough valid documents to sample {num_samples}.&quot;)\n    return sampled_documents</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0253","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-034-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"What does the question prompt (<code>QUESTION_GEN_PROMPT</code>) ask the LLM to write?","a":"<p>A short, first-person, search-engine-style question that can be answered with a specific, concise piece of information from the context. It is phrased as an adult mentee seeking advice from a trusted mentor.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0254","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-034-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"What does the answer prompt (<code>ANSWER_GEN_PROMPT</code>) tell the LLM to do?","a":"<p>Answer the mentee's question in second person, using only the context (\"raw thoughts\") and not prior knowledge.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0255","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-034-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"What does <code>GROUNDEDNESS_PROMPT</code> ask the critic LLM for?","a":"<p>A \"total rating\" from 1 to 5 for how clearly the question can be answered using the context. 1 means not answerable and 5 means clearly answerable. The format is \"Evaluation: (rationale)\" then \"Total rating: (a number in the range 1-5)\".</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>GROUNDEDNESS_PROMPT = &quot;&quot;&quot;You are given context and a question. Provide a &#x27;total rating&#x27; from 1 to 5 indicating \nthe extent to which the question can be answered clearly using the context. 1 = not answerable, 5 = clearly answerable\nFormat your response as:\nEvaluation: (rationale)\nTotal rating: (a number in the range 1-5)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0256","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-034-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"What is <code>HYPE_ANSWER_GEN_PROMPT</code> and where is it used?","a":"<p>It is defined in <code>helpers/prompts.py</code>. It is the same as <code>ANSWER_GEN_PROMPT</code> plus an instruction to answer in a hype, \"OG mentor who has been there\" tone. It is used for the HyDE-style technique in section 6.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0257","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-034-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"How do you turn the prompt strings into LlamaIndex prompt templates?","a":"<p>Wrap each one in <code>PromptTemplate</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>QUESTION_GEN_PROMPT_TEMPLATE = PromptTemplate(QUESTION_GEN_PROMPT)\nANSWER_GEN_PROMPT_TEMPLATE = PromptTemplate(ANSWER_GEN_PROMPT)\nGROUNDEDNESS_PROMPT_TEMPLATE = PromptTemplate(GROUNDEDNESS_PROMPT)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0258","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-034-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"How do you generate one question per chunk in the evaluation-set code?","a":"<p>Loop over the chunks, format the question prompt with the chunk text as context, call <code>llm.complete</code>, and store the question with its context.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for doc in docs_for_eval_set:\n    result_dict = {}\n    context = doc.get_content()\n    prompt = QUESTION_GEN_PROMPT_TEMPLATE.format(context_str=context)\n    response = llm.complete(prompt)\n    result_dict[&#x27;question&#x27;] = response.text\n    result_dict[&quot;context&quot;] = context\n    questions.append(result_dict)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0259","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-034-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"How do you generate an answer from a question plus its context?","a":"<p>Format the answer prompt with <code>query_str</code> and <code>context_str</code>, call the LLM and save the text as <code>answer</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for question in questions:\n    prompt = ANSWER_GEN_PROMPT_TEMPLATE.format(query_str=question[&#x27;question&#x27;], context_str=question[&#x27;context&#x27;])\n    response = llm.complete(prompt)\n    question[&#x27;answer&#x27;] = response.text</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0260","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-035-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"Which model plays the critic that rates how answerable each question is?","a":"<p>A stronger model than the one writing the questions: <code>OpenAI(model=\"gpt-4o\")</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>critic_llm = OpenAI(model=&quot;gpt-4o&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0261","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-035-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"How does the critic code read the score and rationale from the response?","a":"<p>It splits the response text on \"Total rating: \" for the integer score and on \"Evaluation: \" for the rationale. On any exception both fields are set to <code>None</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>score_as_int = int(response_string.split(&quot;Total rating: &quot;)[-1].strip())\nscore_rational = response_string.split(&quot;Total rating: &quot;)[-2].split(&quot;Evaluation: &quot;)[1]\nquestion[&#x27;question_groundedness_score&#x27;] = score_as_int\nquestion[&#x27;question_groundedness_score_rationale&#x27;] = score_rational</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0262","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-035-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"How do you filter the evaluation set for higher quality, and what are its final fields?","a":"<p>Filter on the groundedness score, for example keep score of 4 or more. The final fields are <code>question</code>, <code>context</code>, <code>answer</code>, <code>question_groundedness_score</code> and <code>question_groundedness_score_rationale</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0263","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-035-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"How do you publish the evaluation dataset to the Hugging Face Hub and reuse it?","a":"<p>Build a <code>Dataset</code> from the list, call <code>push_to_hub</code>, and later <code>load_dataset</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>rag_eval_set = Dataset.from_list(questions)\nrag_eval_set.push_to_hub(&quot;harpreetsahota/LI_Learning_RAG_Eval_Set&quot;)\nrag_eval_set = load_dataset(&quot;harpreetsahota/LI_Learning_RAG_Eval_Set&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0264","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-035-5-3-building-an-evaluation-set-synthetic","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s028","q":"What does <code>run_generations_on_eval_set</code> do, and why does it sleep?","a":"<p>It runs the query pipeline on each <code>question</code> and adds <code>response.response</code> as a new dataset column. It sleeps 25 s after every 5 queries to respect the free-tier rate limit.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def run_generations_on_eval_set(eval_dataset, col_name, query_pipeline, time_out=True):\n    responses = []\n    for i, row in tqdm(enumerate(eval_dataset), total=len(eval_dataset), desc=&quot;Generating answers&quot;):\n        response = query_pipeline.run(row[&#x27;question&#x27;])\n        responses.append(response.response)\n        if time_out and (i + 1) % 5 == 0:\n            time.sleep(25)\n    return eval_dataset.add_column(col_name, responses)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0265","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-036-6-1-three-rag-paradigms-from-the-rag-for","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s029","q":"What are the three RAG paradigms in the \"RAG for LLMs: A Survey\" paper?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Paradigm</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Naive RAG</strong></td><td>Index (clean, extract, chunk, vectorize), retrieve (similarity between query and chunks), generate (query + docs into a prompt)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Advanced RAG</strong></td><td>Pre-retrieval and post-retrieval improvements</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Modular RAG</strong></td><td>Adds modules (search module, memory module), allows serialized pipelines or end-to-end training across modules, builds on Advanced RAG</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0266","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-036-6-1-three-rag-paradigms-from-the-rag-for","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s029","q":"What does Advanced RAG improve before and after retrieval?","a":"<p><strong>Pre-retrieval:</strong> better indexing (granularity, structure, metadata, alignment, mixed retrieval), fine-tuned or dynamic embeddings. <strong>Post-retrieval:</strong> re-ranking (diversity, best-document placement, recomputed similarity) and prompt compression (importance estimation, summarization).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0267","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-036-6-1-three-rag-paradigms-from-the-rag-for","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s029","q":"What are the pre-retrieval optimization techniques in Advanced RAG?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Data granularity: standardize text, remove ambiguity, domain annotations.</li>\n  <li>Index structure: varied chunk sizes, multiple index paths, graphs.</li>\n  <li><strong>Metadata</strong> (dates, chapters) for filtering.</li>\n  <li>Alignment: hypothetical questions matched to document content.</li>\n  <li><strong>Mixed retrieval</strong>: keyword + semantic + vector.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0268","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-036-6-1-three-rag-paradigms-from-the-rag-for","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s029","q":"What embedding optimizations does Advanced RAG use?","a":"<p>Fine-tuning embedding models for the domain (not covered in the course), and dynamic embeddings that adapt to context.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0269","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-036-6-1-three-rag-paradigms-from-the-rag-for","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s029","q":"What are the post-retrieval and pipeline optimizations in Advanced RAG?","a":"<p>Post-retrieval: re-ranking, and prompt compression to cut noise. Pipeline: hybrid search, recursive retrieval and query engines (start small, expand), <strong>step-back prompting</strong> (broader reasoning), and <strong>sub-queries and HyDE</strong>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0270","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-037-6-1-three-rag-paradigms-from-the-rag-for","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s029","q":"What is the course map for sections 6 to 8 of the LlamaIndex RAG course?","a":"<p>Pre-retrieval (chunk size, small-to-big, semantic chunking, metadata, document summary index, query transformations), then post-retrieval (node post-processing, reranking, FLARE, prompt compression, self-correcting), then modular (hybrid retrievers, agentic RAG, ensemble retrieval, ensemble query engine).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0271","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-037-6-1-three-rag-paradigms-from-the-rag-for","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s029","q":"How is the LLM set up in the shared notebook setup for advanced RAG?","a":"<p>With <code>setup_llm</code>, using OpenAI <code>gpt-4o</code>, temperature 0.75 and a system prompt that says to use only the provided context.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>setup_llm(\n    provider=&quot;openai&quot;,\n    api_key=OPENAI_API_KEY,\n    model=&quot;gpt-4o&quot;,\n    temperature=0.75,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0272","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-037-6-1-three-rag-paradigms-from-the-rag-for","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s029","q":"How is the embedding model set up in the shared notebook setup?","a":"<p>With <code>setup_embed_model</code> using OpenAI <code>text-embedding-3-small</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>setup_embed_model(provider=&quot;openai&quot;, model=&quot;text-embedding-3-small&quot;, api_key=OPENAI_API_KEY)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0273","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-037-6-1-three-rag-paradigms-from-the-rag-for","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s029","q":"Why do some notebooks use <code>QDRANT_URL = \":memory:\"</code>?","a":"<p>To keep the vector store local.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0274","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-037-6-1-three-rag-paradigms-from-the-rag-for","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s029","q":"How does every advanced RAG notebook end?","a":"<p><code>create_index(from_where=\"vector_store\", ...)</code>, then <code>create_query_engine(...)</code>, optionally <code>update_prompts({'response_synthesizer:text_qa_template': ...})</code>, then <code>create_query_pipeline([InputComponent(), query_engine]).run(input=...)</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0275","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-037-6-1-three-rag-paradigms-from-the-rag-for","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s029","q":"What is <code>HYPE_ANSWER_GEN_PROMPT</code> in the advanced RAG notebooks?","a":"<p>The QA template used in most notebooks, from <code>helpers/prompts.py</code>. It is <code>ANSWER_GEN_PROMPT</code> plus \"speak as an OG mentor who has been there and done that, HYPE tone, be straight up; answer must come from the raw thoughts, not prior knowledge\".</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0276","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-038-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"What is the chunking commandment from Greg Kamradt?","a":"<p>Don't chunk for chunking's sake. Get data into a form that can be retrieved for value later.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0277","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-038-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"Why is chunk size the lowest-hanging fruit for tuning RAG, and what are LlamaIndex's defaults?","a":"<p>Chunk size affects response time, faithfulness and relevancy. LlamaIndex defaults to <strong>chunk size 1024 tokens and overlap 20</strong>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0278","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-038-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"What is the effect of smaller vs larger chunks, and of overlap?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Smaller chunks (e.g., 128)</td><td>More precise, focused embeddings; granular but may lack context</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Larger chunks (e.g., 512+)</td><td>Broader context, good for overviews; may include irrelevant text, miss detail</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Overlap</td><td>Shared tokens between neighbors preserve context across boundaries</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0279","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-038-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"How should you change <code>similarity_top_k</code> when you shrink the chunk size?","a":"<p>Raise it to compensate. Halving 1024 to 512 means retrieving more chunks.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0280","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-038-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"How do <code>TokenTextSplitter</code> and <code>SentenceSplitter</code> differ?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>TokenTextSplitter</th><th>SentenceSplitter</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Splits by</td><td>Token count</td><td>Sentence boundaries</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Sentences preserved</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Chunk length</td><td>Uniform</td><td>Varies</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Use when</td><td>Strict token limits</td><td>Sentence context matters</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0281","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-038-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"What tokenizer does <code>TokenTextSplitter</code> use by default, and what does <code>SentenceSplitter</code> use to find sentences?","a":"<p><code>TokenTextSplitter</code> uses the <code>cl100k_base</code> tokenizer by default. <code>SentenceSplitter</code> keeps sentences and paragraphs whole using NLTK Punkt, so chunk sizes vary.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0282","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-038-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"How do you count the tokens in a string with <code>tiktoken</code>?","a":"<p>Get the <code>cl100k_base</code> encoding and take the length of the encoded string.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>encoding = tiktoken.get_encoding(&quot;cl100k_base&quot;)\ndef num_tokens_from_string(string: str, encoding=encoding) -&gt; int:\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;Returns the number of tokens in a text string.&quot;&quot;&quot;\n    return len(encoding.encode(string))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0283","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-038-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"How do you split a text into 64-token chunks with 16 tokens of overlap using <code>TokenTextSplitter</code>?","a":"<p>Create the splitter and call <code>split_text</code>. The first chunk then counts 64 tokens.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>example_split = TokenTextSplitter(chunk_size=64, chunk_overlap=16).split_text(senpai_documents[42].text)\nnum_tokens_from_string(example_split[0])      # 64</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0284","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-038-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"How do you write token and sentence splitter helpers to compare chunk sizes?","a":"<p>Each helper builds the splitter and calls <code>get_nodes_from_documents</code>. Smaller chunk size gives more chunks.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def token_splitter(chunk_size, documents):\n    splitter = TokenTextSplitter(chunk_size=chunk_size, chunk_overlap=16)\n    return splitter.get_nodes_from_documents(documents)\n\ndef sentence_splitter(chunk_size, documents):\n    splitter = SentenceSplitter(chunk_size=chunk_size, chunk_overlap=16)\n    return splitter.get_nodes_from_documents(documents)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0285","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-039-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"How do you ingest documents with 256-token sentence chunks into a vector store?","a":"<p>Create a <code>SentenceSplitter</code> and pass it with the embed model to <code>ingest</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>sent_splitter = SentenceSplitter(chunk_size=256, chunk_overlap=16)\nsplit_nodes = ingest(\n    documents=senpai_documents,\n    transformations=[sent_splitter, Settings.embed_model],\n    vector_store=vector_store\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0286","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-039-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"How is a query engine configured with compact synthesis and MMR in the chunk-size notebook?","a":"<p>Set <code>response_mode=\"compact\"</code>, a top-k of 5, <code>vector_store_query_mode=\"mmr\"</code> and an <code>mmr_threshold</code> of 0.42.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query_engine = create_query_engine(\n    index=index,\n    mode=&quot;query&quot;,\n    response_mode=&quot;compact&quot;,           # default is &quot;refine&quot; (one LLM call per chunk)\n    similiarty_top_k=5,                # (sic) spelled this way in the course notebooks\n    vector_store_query_mode=&quot;mmr&quot;,\n    vector_store_kwargs={&quot;mmr_threshold&quot;: 0.42}\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0287","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-039-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"What is the default <code>response_mode</code>, and what does it cost?","a":"<p>The default is <code>\"refine\"</code>, which makes one LLM call per chunk. <code>\"compact\"</code> is used instead in the notebooks.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0288","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-039-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"What is the <code>similiarty_top_k</code> gotcha in the course notebooks?","a":"<p>The notebooks misspell it. The correct retriever argument is <code>similarity_top_k</code>. The misspelled keyword is silently passed through as a kwarg, so the default (2) may be what actually applies.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0289","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-039-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"What is the default <code>similarity_top_k</code>?","a":"<p>2.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0290","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-039-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"How do you swap the QA prompt of a query engine for a custom prompt?","a":"<p>Call <code>update_prompts</code> with the <code>response_synthesizer:text_qa_template</code> key.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query_engine.update_prompts({&#x27;response_synthesizer:text_qa_template&#x27;: PromptTemplate(ANSWER_GEN_PROMPT)})</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0291","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-039-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"What is MMR (Maximal Marginal Relevance)?","a":"<p>A method that balances relevance and diversity. It iteratively picks items that are relevant to the query but different from the items already selected.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0292","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-039-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"What is the MMR formula, and what does λ do?","a":"<p><code>MMR = argmax [ λ · Relevance(item, query) − (1 − λ) · max Similarity(item, selected) ]</code>. λ near 1 favors relevance and near 0 favors diversity. <code>mmr_threshold</code> is λ.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0293","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-039-6-2-optimizing-chunk-size","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s030","q":"How do you enable MMR in LlamaIndex, and why does chunk size affect it?","a":"<p>Set <code>vector_store_query_mode=\"mmr\"</code>. MMR depends on embeddings, so chunk size affects it.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0294","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-040-6-3-small-to-big-retrieval-recursive-ret","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s031","q":"What is small-to-big retrieval (recursive retrieval)?","a":"<p>Retrieve small, query-specific chunks, then follow references to larger parent chunks (or inject surrounding context) so the LLM gets both precision and context.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0295","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-040-6-3-small-to-big-retrieval-recursive-ret","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s031","q":"What are the three parts of small-to-big retrieval in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Recursive retrieval, node post-processing and response synthesis.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0296","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-040-6-3-small-to-big-retrieval-recursive-ret","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s031","q":"How does <code>SentenceWindowNodeParser</code> work?","a":"<p>It makes one node per sentence and stores a window of surrounding sentences in metadata (<code>window_size</code> sentences each side; the sentence itself is under <code>original_text</code>). Both are excluded from what the embedding model and LLM see by default, so only the single sentence is embedded. Splitting uses NLTK Punkt.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0297","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-040-6-3-small-to-big-retrieval-recursive-ret","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s031","q":"What does <code>MetadataReplacementPostProcessor</code> do in the sentence window technique?","a":"<p>At query time it swaps the sentence for its window before the LLM sees it.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0298","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-040-6-3-small-to-big-retrieval-recursive-ret","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s031","q":"How do you create a sentence window parser with metadata keys and get nodes?","a":"<p>Pass <code>window_size</code>, <code>window_metadata_key</code> and <code>original_text_metadata_key</code> to <code>SentenceWindowNodeParser</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def sentence_window_splitter(window_size, documents):\n    splitter = SentenceWindowNodeParser(\n        window_size=window_size,\n        window_metadata_key=&quot;window_size&quot;,\n        original_text_metadata_key=&quot;original_text&quot;,\n    )\n    return splitter.get_nodes_from_documents(documents)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0299","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-040-6-3-small-to-big-retrieval-recursive-ret","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s031","q":"How do you see what is stored in a sentence window node vs what the LLM sees?","a":"<p>Print the node content with different metadata modes: <code>\"all\"</code> for what is stored and <code>\"llm\"</code> for what the LLM sees.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>print(nodes[5].get_content(metadata_mode=&quot;all&quot;))   # what is stored\nprint(nodes[5].get_content(metadata_mode=&quot;llm&quot;))   # what the LLM sees</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0300","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-040-6-3-small-to-big-retrieval-recursive-ret","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s031","q":"Why does <code>ingest</code> only embed in the sentence window notebook?","a":"<p>The parser already split the documents, so the transformations list holds only the embed model.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>split_nodes = ingest(documents=nodes, transformations=[Settings.embed_model],\n                     vector_store=sentence_window_vector_store)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0301","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-040-6-3-small-to-big-retrieval-recursive-ret","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s031","q":"How do you plug <code>MetadataReplacementPostProcessor</code> into a query engine?","a":"<p>Make a postprocessor with <code>target_metadata_key=\"window\"</code> and pass it in <code>node_postprocessors</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>node_postprocessors = [MetadataReplacementPostProcessor(target_metadata_key=&quot;window&quot;)]\n    node_postprocessors=node_postprocessors</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0302","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-040-6-3-small-to-big-retrieval-recursive-ret","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s031","q":"What key mismatch exists in the sentence window notebook?","a":"<p>The notebook sets <code>window_metadata_key=\"window_size\"</code> while the post-processor targets <code>\"window\"</code> (the parser's default key). Keep the keys consistent when you write your own.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0303","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-040-6-3-small-to-big-retrieval-recursive-ret","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s031","q":"How does the parent-child option (Option B) of small-to-big retrieval work?","a":"<p>Smaller child chunks (several sizes) point to a bigger parent via <code>IndexNode</code>. Retrieval matches a small child, then follows the reference to the parent.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0304","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-040-6-3-small-to-big-retrieval-recursive-ret","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s031","q":"How do you build child chunks of several sizes that reference their parent?","a":"<p>Make one <code>SentenceSplitter</code> per sub chunk size, split each base node, and create <code>IndexNode</code>s from the child text nodes with the parent's node id.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>sub_chunk_sizes = [128, 256, 512]\nsub_node_parsers = [SentenceSplitter(chunk_size=c, chunk_overlap=16) for c in sub_chunk_sizes]\n        sub_inodes = [IndexNode.from_text_node(sn, base_node.node_id) for sn in sub_nodes]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0305","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-041-6-3-small-to-big-retrieval-recursive-ret","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s031","q":"How is the parent itself indexed in parent-child retrieval, and what dict is built for resolving references?","a":"<p>The parent is also indexed as an <code>IndexNode</code>, and a dict maps each node id to its node.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>original_node = IndexNode.from_text_node(base_node, base_node.node_id)\nall_nodes.append(original_node)\nall_nodes_dict = {n.node_id: n for n in all_nodes}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0306","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-041-6-3-small-to-big-retrieval-recursive-ret","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s031","q":"What is <code>RecursiveRetriever</code>, and how is it different from a normal retriever?","a":"<p>It is not created via <code>index.as_retriever()</code>. It is a standalone class that takes a root id plus dicts of retrievers, query engines and nodes, follows links, deduplicates nodes and returns them.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0307","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-041-6-3-small-to-big-retrieval-recursive-ret","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s031","q":"What is <code>RetrieverQueryEngine</code>?","a":"<p>A query engine that wraps a retriever, applies postprocessing and synthesizes the answer.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0308","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-041-6-3-small-to-big-retrieval-recursive-ret","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s031","q":"How do you build a <code>RecursiveRetriever</code> for parent-child retrieval and wrap it in a query engine?","a":"<p>Give it the root id <code>\"vector\"</code>, the retriever dict and the node dict, then wrap it with <code>RetrieverQueryEngine.from_args</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>retriever_chunk = RecursiveRetriever(\n    &quot;vector&quot;,                                        # root id\n    retriever_dict={&quot;vector&quot;: parent_child_retriever},\n    node_dict=all_nodes_dict,                        # id → node, used to resolve references\n    verbose=True,\n)\nparent_child_query_engine = RetrieverQueryEngine.from_args(retriever_chunk, llm=Settings.llm)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0309","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-041-6-3-small-to-big-retrieval-recursive-ret","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s031","q":"What is the comparison of sentence window vs parent-child small-to-big techniques?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Technique</th><th>How it works</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>SentenceWindowNodeParser</code> + <code>MetadataReplacementPostProcessor</code></td><td>Embed one sentence, give the LLM its surrounding window</td><td>Sentence-level precision with wider context</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Parent-child <code>IndexNode</code>s + <code>RecursiveRetriever</code></td><td>Match small chunks, follow references to the parent</td><td>Multi-granularity, hierarchical content</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0310","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-042-6-4-semantic-chunking","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s032","q":"What is semantic chunking?","a":"<p>Instead of fixed N tokens or sentences, use <strong>embeddings to find breakpoints</strong> where meaning shifts (popularized by Greg Kamradt). It keeps related sentences together, and chunk size is dynamic.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0311","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-042-6-4-semantic-chunking","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s032","q":"How does <code>SemanticSplitterNodeParser</code> work, step by step?","a":"<p>(1) Split into sentences (default <code>split_by_sentence_tokenizer</code>, NLTK Punkt). (2) Group adjacent sentences by <code>buffer_size</code> (1 means each sentence alone). (3) Embed each group. (4) Take the cosine similarity between adjacent groups and convert it to distance (1 − similarity). (5) Make a breakpoint where the distance exceeds the <code>breakpoint_percentile_threshold</code> percentile. (6) Sentences between breakpoints become one node.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0312","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-042-6-4-semantic-chunking","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s032","q":"What are the arguments of <code>SemanticSplitterNodeParser</code> and their defaults?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Argument</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>embed_model</code></td><td>Model used for similarity</td><td>from Settings</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>buffer_size</code></td><td>Sentences grouped together when comparing</td><td>1</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>breakpoint_percentile_threshold</code></td><td>Percentile of distances that triggers a split; lower gives more nodes</td><td>95</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>sentence_splitter</code></td><td>Pre-splitter</td><td><code>split_by_sentence_tokenizer</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0313","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-042-6-4-semantic-chunking","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s032","q":"What design choices can you experiment with in semantic chunking?","a":"<p>The embedding model and its dimensions, buffer size, breakpoint threshold and sentence splitter.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0314","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-042-6-4-semantic-chunking","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s032","q":"How do you create semantic nodes with <code>SemanticSplitterNodeParser</code>?","a":"<p>Pass the embed model, buffer size and breakpoint percentile threshold, then call <code>get_nodes_from_documents</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>splitter = SemanticSplitterNodeParser(\n    embed_model=embed_model,\n    buffer_size=buffer_size,\n    breakpoint_percentile_threshold=breakpoint_percentile_threshold,\n)\nreturn splitter.get_nodes_from_documents(documents)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0315","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-042-6-4-semantic-chunking","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s032","q":"Why does the semantic chunking notebook keep Qdrant in memory?","a":"<p>Embedding every sentence group is slow (about 30 minutes in the notebook).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>semantic_nodes_vector_store = setup_vector_store(&quot;:memory:&quot;, QDRANT_API_KEY, &quot;words-of-the-senpai-semantic-nodes&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0316","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-042-6-4-semantic-chunking","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s032","q":"How can you set the QA prompt without <code>update_prompts()</code>?","a":"<p>Pass <code>text_qa_template</code> directly to <code>create_query_engine</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>text_qa_template=HYPE_ANSWER_GEN_PROMPT_TEMPLATE      # alternative to update_prompts()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0317","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-042-6-4-semantic-chunking","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s032","q":"How do fixed and semantic chunking compare?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Fixed chunking</th><th>Semantic chunking</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Breakpoints</td><td>Fixed N tokens/sentences</td><td>Where similarity drops</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Related sentences</td><td>May be split</td><td>Kept together</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Cost</td><td>Fast</td><td>Slower (embeds sentence groups)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Simple docs, speed</td><td>Complex docs, retrieval accuracy</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0318","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-043-6-5-metadata-extraction","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s033","q":"Why add metadata to chunks?","a":"<p>Chunks can look alike. Metadata disambiguates them and enables filtering. Effectiveness depends on the quality of the tags.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0319","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-043-6-5-metadata-extraction","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s033","q":"How do you add manual metadata to documents?","a":"<p>Add a dict entry per document, here a <code>known_for</code> description looked up by author.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>for document in senpai_documents:\n    document.metadata[&#x27;known_for&#x27;] = known_for.get(document.metadata[&#x27;author&#x27;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0320","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-043-6-5-metadata-extraction","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s033","q":"What are the four automatic metadata extractors in LlamaIndex and what does each add?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Extractor</th><th>Adds</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>SummaryExtractor</code></td><td>Summary of the node, optionally of previous/next nodes (<code>summaries=[\"prev\",\"self\",\"next\"]</code>)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>QuestionsAnsweredExtractor</code></td><td>Questions the node can answer (<code>questions=N</code>)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>TitleExtractor</code></td><td>A title over node context (<code>nodes=5</code>)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>KeywordExtractor</code></td><td>Unique keywords, comma separated (<code>keywords=10</code>)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0321","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-043-6-5-metadata-extraction","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s033","q":"How do automatic extractors run?","a":"<p>They use an LLM and run as transformations in the ingestion pipeline.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0322","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-043-6-5-metadata-extraction","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s033","q":"How do you inspect the prompt of an extractor?","a":"<p>Print <code>prompt_template</code> for <code>SummaryExtractor</code> and <code>QuestionsAnsweredExtractor</code>, and <code>node_template</code> for <code>TitleExtractor</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>print(SummaryExtractor().prompt_template)\nprint(QuestionsAnsweredExtractor().prompt_template)\nprint(TitleExtractor().node_template)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0323","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-043-6-5-metadata-extraction","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s033","q":"How do you create a <code>QuestionsAnsweredExtractor</code> so the embedding model sees the metadata?","a":"<p>Pass <code>questions=2</code>, an LLM and <code>metadata_mode=MetadataMode.EMBED</code> (metadata visible to the embedding model).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>qa_extractor = QuestionsAnsweredExtractor(\n    questions=2,\n    llm=qa_llm,\n    metadata_mode=MetadataMode.EMBED,       # metadata visible to the embedding model\n    embed_model=Settings.embed_model,\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0324","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-043-6-5-metadata-extraction","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s033","q":"How do you create a <code>SummaryExtractor</code> that summarizes the previous, current and next nodes?","a":"<p>Pass <code>summaries=[\"prev\", \"self\", \"next\"]</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>summary_extractor = SummaryExtractor(summaries=[&quot;prev&quot;, &quot;self&quot;, &quot;next&quot;], llm=qa_llm)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0325","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-043-6-5-metadata-extraction","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s033","q":"How do you create keyword and title extractors?","a":"<p><code>KeywordExtractor(keywords=10, ...)</code> and <code>TitleExtractor(nodes=5, ...)</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>keyword_extractor = KeywordExtractor(keywords=10, llm=llm)      # other options to try\ntitle_extractor = TitleExtractor(nodes=5, llm=llm)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0326","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-043-6-5-metadata-extraction","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s033","q":"How do splitting, extraction and embedding happen together in one ingestion pipeline?","a":"<p>Put them all in the transformations list of <code>ingest</code>: splitter, extractors, then the embed model.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>transforms = [text_splitter, qa_extractor, summary_extractor, Settings.embed_model]\nqa_summaries = ingest(\n    documents=senpai_documents,\n    transformations=transforms,\n    vector_store=qa_summaries_vector_store      # collection &quot;words-of-the-senpai-qa-plus-summaries-nodes&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0327","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-043-6-5-metadata-extraction","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s033","q":"What design choices matter for metadata extraction, and what is the cost?","a":"<p>Which extractors to use, the extraction LLM (gpt-4o quality vs gpt-3.5-turbo cost), questions per node, summary scope, splitter, and chunk size and overlap. More metadata means a slower, costlier ingestion.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0328","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-044-6-6-document-summary-index","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s034","q":"What is the Document Summary Index, and which limits of chunk-only retrieval does it address?","a":"<p>It embeds <strong>document summaries</strong> and links them to their chunks. Chunk-only retrieval has these limits: chunks lack global context, similarity thresholds need tuning, embeddings may miss relevance, and keyword filtering has its own problems.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0329","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-044-6-6-document-summary-index","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s034","q":"What does a Document Summary Index store, and how does retrieval work?","a":"<p>It stores an LLM summary per document, the document's text chunks, and a mapping between them. Retrieval operates at the document level first, then synthesizes over the linked chunks (different optimal representations for retrieval vs synthesis).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0330","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-044-6-6-document-summary-index","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s034","q":"How do you build a <code>DocumentSummaryIndex</code>?","a":"<p>Call <code>DocumentSummaryIndex.from_documents</code> with the LLM, embed model, a splitter and a <code>tree_summarize</code> response synthesizer that generates each document's summary.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>response_synthesizer = get_response_synthesizer(response_mode=&quot;tree_summarize&quot;, use_async=True)\n\ndoc_summary_index = DocumentSummaryIndex.from_documents(\n    senpai_documents,\n    llm=Settings.llm,\n    embed_model=Settings.embed_model,\n    transformations=[splitter],\n    response_synthesizer=response_synthesizer,     # generates each document&#x27;s summary\n    show_progress=True,\n    vector_store=doc_summary_vector_store          # collection &quot;words-of-the-senpai-document-summary-index&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0331","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-044-6-6-document-summary-index","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s034","q":"Which retrieval does <code>as_query_engine()</code> use on a Document Summary Index by default?","a":"<p><strong>Embedding-based</strong> retrieval. The low-level retrievers allow either mode.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0332","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-044-6-6-document-summary-index","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s034","q":"What are the differences between the LLM-based and embedding-based Document Summary Index retrievers?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>LLM-based (<code>DocumentSummaryIndexLLMRetriever</code>)</th><th>Embedding-based (<code>DocumentSummaryIndexEmbeddingRetriever</code>)</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Selects by</td><td>LLM scores summaries in batches (<code>choice_batch_size</code>, default 10; <code>choice_top_k</code>, default 1)</td><td>Cosine similarity of query vs summary embeddings (<code>similarity_top_k</code>)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Speed / cost</td><td>Slower, more expensive</td><td>Faster, cheaper</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Quality</td><td>Higher via LLM reasoning</td><td>Depends on embedding quality</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Custom hooks</td><td><code>choice_select_prompt</code>, <code>format_node_batch_fn</code>, <code>parse_choice_select_answer_fn</code></td><td><code>similarity_top_k</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0333","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-044-6-6-document-summary-index","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s034","q":"How do you create the LLM-based Document Summary Index retriever and query engine?","a":"<p>Create <code>DocumentSummaryIndexLLMRetriever</code> with <code>choice_top_k</code> and the LLM, then wrap it with <code>RetrieverQueryEngine</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>doc_llm_retriever = DocumentSummaryIndexLLMRetriever(\n    doc_summary_index,\n    choice_top_k=5,\n    llm=Settings.llm,\n)\ndoc_llm_query_engine = RetrieverQueryEngine(\n    retriever=doc_llm_retriever, response_synthesizer=response_synthesizer)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0334","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-044-6-6-document-summary-index","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s034","q":"How do you create the embedding-based Document Summary Index retriever and query engine?","a":"<p>Create <code>DocumentSummaryIndexEmbeddingRetriever</code> from the index, then wrap it with <code>RetrieverQueryEngine</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>doc_embed_retriever = DocumentSummaryIndexEmbeddingRetriever(\n    doc_summary_index,\n)\ndoc_embed_query_engine = RetrieverQueryEngine(\n    retriever=doc_embed_retriever, response_synthesizer=response_synthesizer)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0335","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-044-6-6-document-summary-index","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s034","q":"Do the Document Summary Index retrievers support changes to the index?","a":"<p>Yes, they support adding and deleting documents from the index.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0336","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-045-6-7-query-transformations","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s035","q":"What are query transformations, and what three techniques does the course cover?","a":"<p>They rewrite or decompose the user query <strong>before</strong> retrieval. The three techniques are query expansion or rewriting, <code>SubQuestionQueryEngine</code>, and HyDE.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0337","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-045-6-7-query-transformations","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s035","q":"How does query expansion (rewriting) work?","a":"<p>An LLM produces several alternate queries from a few-shot prompt, and each one is sent for retrieval.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0338","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-045-6-7-query-transformations","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s035","q":"What does the query expansion prompt tell the LLM to do?","a":"<p>Understand the essence of the user query and produce <code>{num_queries}</code> alternate queries that expand it so it is more robust, one per line, so the user receives the most relevant information.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0339","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-045-6-7-query-transformations","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s035","q":"How do you call the LLM to expand a query into alternate queries?","a":"<p>Use <code>llm.predict</code> with the template, <code>num_queries</code> and <code>query</code>, then split the response on newlines.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def generate_queries(query=QUERY_STRING, llm=Settings.llm, num_queries=4):\n    response = llm.predict(QUERY_GEN_PROMPT_TEMPLATE, num_queries=num_queries, query=query)\n    queries = response.split(&quot;\\n&quot;)\n    print(&quot;Generated queries:\\n&quot; + &quot;\\n&quot;.join(queries))\n    return queries</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0340","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-045-6-7-query-transformations","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s035","q":"What is <code>SubQuestionQueryEngine</code>?","a":"<p>It decomposes a complex query into sub-questions, each aimed at a specific data source (a <code>QueryEngineTool</code>), runs them, then synthesizes the final answer. It suits compare and contrast, multi-part, and multi-document questions.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0341","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-045-6-7-query-transformations","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s035","q":"How do you wrap a query engine as a tool for <code>SubQuestionQueryEngine</code>?","a":"<p>Use <code>QueryEngineTool</code> with <code>ToolMetadata</code> holding a name and description.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query_engine_tools = [\n    QueryEngineTool(\n        query_engine=index.as_query_engine(),\n        metadata=ToolMetadata(\n            name=&quot;the senpais&quot;,\n            description=&quot;The collective thoughts and writings of all my virtual mentors&quot;,\n        ),\n    ),\n]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0342","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-045-6-7-query-transformations","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s035","q":"How do you create a <code>SubQuestionQueryEngine</code> from tools?","a":"<p>Call <code>from_defaults</code> with the tools and <code>use_async=True</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>sub_question_query_engine = SubQuestionQueryEngine.from_defaults(\n    query_engine_tools=query_engine_tools,\n    use_async=True\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0343","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-046-6-7-query-transformations","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s035","q":"What is HyDE (Hypothetical Document Embeddings)?","a":"<p>The LLM writes a hypothetical answer, and that text is embedded and used for the search.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0344","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-046-6-7-query-transformations","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s035","q":"Why does HyDE work?","a":"<p>A hypothetical answer is semantically closer to real answers than the question is. The hypothetical document may contain inaccuracies, but the embedding only has to land in the right neighborhood.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0345","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-046-6-7-query-transformations","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s035","q":"Is HyDE zero-shot, and which paper introduced it?","a":"<p>Yes. It needs no labels or fine-tuning and performs comparably to fine-tuned retrievers. The paper is <em>Precise Zero-Shot Dense Retrieval without Relevance Labels</em>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0346","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-046-6-7-query-transformations","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s035","q":"How do you use HyDE in LlamaIndex, and what does <code>include_original=True</code> do?","a":"<p>Create <code>HyDEQueryTransform</code> and wrap the query engine in <code>TransformQueryEngine</code>. <code>include_original=True</code> also keeps the original query embedding.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>hyde = HyDEQueryTransform(include_original=True)     # also keep the original query embedding\nhyde_query_engine = TransformQueryEngine(\n    query_engine=index.as_query_engine(),\n    query_transform=hyde,\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0347","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-046-6-7-query-transformations","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s035","q":"When do you use query expansion, <code>SubQuestionQueryEngine</code> and HyDE?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Technique</th><th>Use when</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Query expansion</td><td>Users articulate poorly; you need broader recall</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>SubQuestionQueryEngine</code></td><td>Multi-part or cross-source questions</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>HyDE</td><td>Vague or broad queries; better query-document embedding alignment</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0348","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-047-7-advanced-rag-post-retrieval-other-tech","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s036","q":"How is the data prepared for the post-retrieval notebooks?","a":"<p>Sample 10 documents per author, chunk with <code>SentenceSplitter(chunk_size=256, chunk_overlap=16)</code>, <code>ingest</code> into an in-memory Qdrant collection (<code>QDRANT_URL = \":memory:\"</code>), then <code>create_index(from_where=\"vector_store\", ...)</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0349","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-047-7-advanced-rag-post-retrieval-other-tech","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s036","q":"What is the order of operations in a LlamaIndex query?","a":"<p>Ingestion, indexing, retrieval, <strong>reranking</strong>, <strong>post-processing</strong>, response generation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0350","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-047-7-advanced-rag-post-retrieval-other-tech","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s036","q":"What is the difference between reranking and post-processing in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Reranking reorders nodes (most relevant first). Post-processing transforms or filters nodes (drop low scores, replace text, compress). Both run on retrieved nodes before the LLM.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0351","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-048-7-1-node-post-processing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s037","q":"What is a node postprocessor in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>A component that takes the retrieved nodes, transforms or filters them and returns them, after retrieval and before response synthesis. All subclass <code>BaseNodePostProcessor</code>, so they share one usage pattern.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0352","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-048-7-1-node-post-processing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s037","q":"Do node postprocessors plug into <code>as_retriever()</code> or into a query engine?","a":"<p>Into a <strong>query engine</strong>, not into <code>as_retriever()</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0353","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-048-7-1-node-post-processing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s037","q":"How do you add a postprocessor to a query engine?","a":"<p>Pass <code>node_postprocessors</code> to <code>as_query_engine</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query_engine = index.as_query_engine(\n    ...,                                  # other query engine arguments\n    node_postprocessors=[your_post_processor]\n)\nresponse = query_engine.query(&quot;your query&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0354","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-048-7-1-node-post-processing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s037","q":"How do you assemble a retriever and a postprocessor manually?","a":"<p>Build a <code>VectorIndexRetriever</code> and pass it with <code>node_postprocessors</code> to <code>RetrieverQueryEngine</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>retriever = VectorIndexRetriever(index=index, similarity_top_k=10)\nquery_engine = RetrieverQueryEngine(\n    retriever=retriever,\n    node_postprocessors=[SimilarityPostprocessor(similarity_cutoff=0.7)]\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0355","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-048-7-1-node-post-processing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s037","q":"How do you filter nodes by similarity score?","a":"<p>Use <code>SimilarityPostprocessor</code> with a <code>similarity_cutoff</code>. It keeps nodes whose score is at least the cutoff.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>similarity_postprocessor = SimilarityPostprocessor(similarity_cutoff=0.7)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0356","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-048-7-1-node-post-processing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s037","q":"How do you filter nodes by keywords?","a":"<p>Use <code>KeywordNodePostprocessor</code> with <code>required_keywords</code> and <code>exclude_keywords</code>. It uses spaCy, and <code>lang</code> defaults to <code>\"en\"</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>keyword_postprocessor = KeywordNodePostprocessor(\n    required_keywords=required_keywords, exclude_keywords=exclude_keywords)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0357","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-048-7-1-node-post-processing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s037","q":"How do you replace node text with a metadata value, and what do you pair it with?","a":"<p>Use <code>MetadataReplacementPostProcessor</code> with <code>target_metadata_key</code>. Pair it with <code>SentenceWindowNodeParser</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>postprocessor = MetadataReplacementPostProcessor(target_metadata_key=&quot;window&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0358","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-049-7-1-node-post-processing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s037","q":"How do you reorder nodes so the best ones sit at the start and the end?","a":"<p>Use <code>LongContextReorder</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>postprocessor = LongContextReorder()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0359","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-049-7-1-node-post-processing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s037","q":"How do you keep only query-relevant sentences inside each node?","a":"<p>Use <code>SentenceEmbeddingOptimizer</code> with the embed model, <code>percentile_cutoff</code> and <code>threshold_cutoff</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>postprocessor = SentenceEmbeddingOptimizer(\n    embed_model=Settings.embed_model,\n    percentile_cutoff=0.5,\n    threshold_cutoff=0.7\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0360","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-049-7-1-node-post-processing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s037","q":"How do you use a keyword postprocessor in the notebook's query engine helper and check the retrieved source nodes?","a":"<p>Pass it as <code>post_processor</code> with <code>return_source=True</code>, then inspect the first source node.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>    post_processor=keyword_postprocessor,\n    return_source=True\nresponse = query_engine.query(&quot;How to make good decisions?&quot;)\nresponse.source_nodes[0].__dict__</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0361","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-049-7-1-node-post-processing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s037","q":"What does each LlamaIndex node postprocessor do under the hood, and what are its key arguments?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Postprocessor</th><th>Under the hood</th><th>Key arguments</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>SimilarityPostprocessor</code></td><td>Keep nodes whose score ≥ cutoff</td><td><code>similarity_cutoff</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>KeywordNodePostprocessor</code></td><td>Skip a node if it lacks required keywords or contains an excluded one (spaCy matching)</td><td><code>required_keywords</code>, <code>exclude_keywords</code>, <code>lang</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>MetadataReplacementPostProcessor</code></td><td>Swap node text for a metadata value</td><td><code>target_metadata_key</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>LongContextReorder</code></td><td>Sort by score desc; even-indexed nodes inserted at the front, odd-indexed appended at the end, so best nodes sit at both ends</td><td>none</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>SentenceEmbeddingOptimizer</code></td><td>Split nodes into sentences, embed, keep top sentences (<code>int(n * percentile_cutoff)</code>) and/or those with similarity ≥ threshold</td><td><code>percentile_cutoff</code>, <code>threshold_cutoff</code>, <code>context_before/after</code>, <code>tokenizer_fn</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0362","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-049-7-1-node-post-processing","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s037","q":"What is \"Lost in the Middle\", and which postprocessor targets it?","a":"<p>LLMs use information at the start or end of a long context best and degrade for facts in the middle (paper: <em>Lost in the Middle: How Language Models Use Long Contexts</em>). <code>LongContextReorder</code> targets this. It is useful when <code>top_k</code> is large.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0363","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-050-7-2-re-ranking","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s038","q":"What is re-ranking in RAG, and what is the usual retrieval pattern?","a":"<p>Reorder retrieved nodes by relevance with a dedicated model. Retrieve many (for example <code>similarity_top_k=15</code>), rerank, and keep the best <code>top_n</code>. Rerankers use the same usage pattern as postprocessors.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0364","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-050-7-2-re-ranking","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s038","q":"How do you create a Cohere reranker in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Use <code>CohereRerank</code> with <code>top_n</code>, the model name and the API key.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>postprocessor = CohereRerank(\n    top_n=5, model=&quot;rerank-english-v3.0&quot;, api_key=CO_API_KEY\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0365","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-050-7-2-re-ranking","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s038","q":"Why is <code>similiarty_top_k=15</code> used together with <code>top_n=5</code> in the rerank notebook?","a":"<p>It over-retrieves 15 nodes, then reranking cuts them to <code>top_n=5</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>    similiarty_top_k=15,          # over-retrieve, then rerank down to top_n=5\n    post_processor=postprocessor,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0366","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-050-7-2-re-ranking","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s038","q":"What are the alternatives to Cohere Rerank, and which is the most popular?","a":"<p><strong>ColBERT rerank</strong> (<code>pip install llama-index-postprocessor-colbert-rerank</code>; <code>from llama_index.postprocessor.colbert_rerank import ColbertRerank</code>) and <strong>Flag Embedding reranker</strong> (<code>pip install llama-index-postprocessor-flag-embedding-reranker</code>; <code>from llama_index.postprocessor.flag_embedding_reranker import FlagEmbeddingReranker</code>). Cohere Rerank is the most popular. All use the same pattern.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0367","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-051-7-3-flare-forward-looking-active-retriev","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s039","q":"What is FLARE?","a":"<p>Forward-Looking Active REtrieval. It retrieves actively during generation, deciding when and what to retrieve (paper: <em>Active Retrieval Augmented Generation</em>). Most RAG retrieves once, which is not enough for long-form generation.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0368","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-051-7-3-flare-forward-looking-active-retriev","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s039","q":"What are the steps of FLARE?","a":"<ol>\n  <li>Predict (look ahead to) the upcoming sentence. 2. Use it as a retrieval query. 3. If it has <strong>low-confidence tokens</strong>, regenerate it with the retrieved documents. 4. Repeat until the response is complete or <code>max_iterations</code> is hit.</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0369","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-051-7-3-flare-forward-looking-active-retriev","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s039","q":"What is the difference between <code>FLAREInstruct</code> and <code>FLAREDirect</code>?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Variant</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>FLAREInstruct</code></td><td>Prompts the LLM with retrieval-encouraging instructions to emit search queries when needed (implemented in LlamaIndex as <code>FLAREInstructQueryEngine</code>)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>FLAREDirect</code></td><td>Uses the LLM's own written sentence as the query if it contains uncertain tokens</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0370","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-051-7-3-flare-forward-looking-active-retriev","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s039","q":"When does FLARE trigger retrieval, and what forms can its queries take?","a":"<p>Confidence-based retrieval triggers only when the model lacks knowledge. Queries can be masked sentences (implicit) or written questions (explicit).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0371","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-051-7-3-flare-forward-looking-active-retriev","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s039","q":"How do you create a <code>FLAREInstructQueryEngine</code>?","a":"<p>Wrap a base query engine and set <code>max_iterations</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>index_query_engine = index.as_query_engine(similarity_top_k=3)\nflare_query_engine = FLAREInstructQueryEngine(\n    query_engine=index_query_engine,\n    max_iterations=7,\n    verbose=True,\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0372","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-051-7-3-flare-forward-looking-active-retriev","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s039","q":"What other options does <code>FLAREInstructQueryEngine</code> have?","a":"<p><code>llm</code>, <code>instruct_prompt</code> and <code>lookahead_answer_inserter</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0373","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-051-7-3-flare-forward-looking-active-retriev","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s039","q":"How do standard RAG and FLARE compare?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Standard RAG</th><th>FLARE</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Retrieval</td><td>Once, before generation</td><td>Repeatedly, when confidence is low</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Hallucination control</td><td>Limited</td><td>Regenerates low-confidence sentences</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>LLM calls</td><td>Fewer</td><td>Many</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Short, focused answers</td><td>Long-form, knowledge-intensive output</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0374","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-052-7-4-prompt-compression-longllmlingua","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s040","q":"What is prompt compression with LongLLMLingua and why use it?","a":"<p>It shortens the prompt while keeping the relevant information: faster, cheaper, and it counters \"lost in the middle\". The reported gain is up to 21.4 points at 4x compression in RAG settings.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0375","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-052-7-4-prompt-compression-longllmlingua","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s040","q":"What are the four components of LongLLMLingua?","a":"<ol>\n  <li><strong>Question-aware coarse-grained compression</strong>: relevance of each context to the question based on perplexity. 2. <strong>Question-aware fine-grained compression</strong>: contrastive perplexity to keep key tokens (not implemented in LlamaIndex). 3. <strong>Adaptive granular control</strong>: different compression ratios per document, driven by the coarse-grained ranking. 4. <strong>Subsequence recovery</strong>: maps response subsequences back to the original prompt content.</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0376","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-052-7-4-prompt-compression-longllmlingua","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s040","q":"How do you create a <code>LongLLMLinguaPostprocessor</code>?","a":"<p>Pass an instruction string, a <code>target_token</code> budget, the rank method and extra compress kwargs.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>node_postprocessor = LongLLMLinguaPostprocessor(\n    instruction_str=&quot;Given the context, please answer the final question&quot;,\n    target_token=300,\n    rank_method=&quot;longllmlingua&quot;,\n    additional_compress_kwargs={\n        &quot;condition_compare&quot;: True,\n        &quot;condition_in_question&quot;: &quot;after&quot;,\n        &quot;context_budget&quot;: &quot;+100&quot;,\n        &quot;reorder_context&quot;: &quot;sort&quot;,                 # enable document reorder\n        &quot;dynamic_context_compression_ratio&quot;: 0.4,  # enable dynamic compression ratio\n    },\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0377","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-052-7-4-prompt-compression-longllmlingua","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s040","q":"What does LongLLMLingua need to run, and what are its defaults?","a":"<p>It requires a GPU. <code>model_name</code> defaults to <code>NousResearch/Llama-2-7b-hf</code> and <code>device_map</code> defaults to <code>\"cuda\"</code>. Other arguments are <code>model_config</code>, <code>open_api_config</code> and <code>metadata_mode</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0378","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-052-7-4-prompt-compression-longllmlingua","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s040","q":"How is <code>LongLLMLinguaPostprocessor</code> used in a query engine?","a":"<p>Like any node postprocessor, through <code>index.as_query_engine(node_postprocessors=[node_postprocessor])</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0379","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-053-7-5-self-correcting-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s041","q":"What is self-correcting RAG?","a":"<p>Query engines that <strong>evaluate their own output and retry</strong> when it isn't good enough.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0380","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-053-7-5-self-correcting-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s041","q":"What are <code>RetryQueryEngine</code>, <code>RetrySourceQueryEngine</code> and <code>RetryGuidelineQueryEngine</code>?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Engine</th><th>Evaluator</th><th>On failure</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>RetryQueryEngine</code></td><td><code>RelevancyEvaluator</code></td><td>Transforms the query using the evaluation result and re-queries, up to <code>max_retries</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>RetrySourceQueryEngine</code></td><td><code>RelevancyEvaluator</code></td><td>Evaluates each source node, builds a new index from only the passing nodes, retries on it</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>RetryGuidelineQueryEngine</code></td><td><code>GuidelineEvaluator</code> (custom guidelines)</td><td>Transforms the query from feedback (<code>FeedbackQueryTransformation</code>, optionally <code>resynthesize_query=True</code>) and retries</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0381","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-053-7-5-self-correcting-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s041","q":"How do you create the retry query engines with a relevancy evaluator?","a":"<p>Create a <code>RelevancyEvaluator</code> and pass it with the base query engine.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query_response_evaluator = RelevancyEvaluator()\n\nretry_query_engine = RetryQueryEngine(base_query_engine, query_response_evaluator)\nretry_source_query_engine = RetrySourceQueryEngine(base_query_engine, query_response_evaluator)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0382","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-053-7-5-self-correcting-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s041","q":"How do you define custom guidelines for <code>GuidelineEvaluator</code>?","a":"<p>Append your own rules to <code>DEFAULT_GUIDELINES</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>guideline_eval = GuidelineEvaluator(\n    guidelines=DEFAULT_GUIDELINES\n    + &quot;\\nThe response should not be overly long.\\n&quot;\n    &quot;The response should try to summarize where possible.\\n&quot;\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0383","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-053-7-5-self-correcting-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s041","q":"How do you try the guideline evaluator and query transform by hand?","a":"<p>Evaluate a response with <code>evaluate_response</code>, then run <code>FeedbackQueryTransformation</code> with the evaluation to get a transformed query.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>eval = guideline_eval.evaluate_response(query, typed_response)\nprint(f&quot;Guideline eval evaluation result: {eval.feedback}&quot;)\n\nfeedback_query_transform = FeedbackQueryTransformation(resynthesize_query=True)\ntransformed_query = feedback_query_transform.run(query, {&quot;evaluation&quot;: eval})\nprint(f&quot;Transformed query: {transformed_query.query_str}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0384","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-053-7-5-self-correcting-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s041","q":"How do you create a <code>RetryGuidelineQueryEngine</code>?","a":"<p>Pass the base query engine, the guideline evaluator and <code>resynthesize_query=True</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>retry_guideline_query_engine = RetryGuidelineQueryEngine(\n    base_query_engine, guideline_eval, resynthesize_query=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0385","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-053-7-5-self-correcting-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s041","q":"What happens with <code>max_retries</code> in the retry engines, and what do retries cost?","a":"<p>Each retry engine takes <code>max_retries</code>. If the response passes evaluation it is returned. If <code>max_retries</code> is 0, the first response is returned unevaluated. Each retry costs extra LLM calls (evaluation plus re-query).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0386","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-054-8-modular-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s042","q":"What is Modular RAG in the LlamaIndex course?","a":"<p>It treats retrieval and generation as composable modules: hybrid retrievers, agents that choose filters, ensembles of retrievers or query engines, and routers. The setup is the same as sections 6 to 7 (10 sampled documents per author, <code>SentenceSplitter(256, 16)</code>).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0387","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-055-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"What is hybrid retrieval?","a":"<p>It combines <strong>vector search</strong> (semantic similarity) with <strong>keyword or full-text search</strong> (BM25).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0388","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-055-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"What are the strengths and weaknesses of vector, keyword (BM25) and hybrid search?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Search</th><th>Strength</th><th>Weakness</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Vector (dense)</td><td>Finds semantically similar text without exact keywords</td><td>Can miss exact keyword matches</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Keyword (BM25)</td><td>Fast exact keyword matching</td><td>Misses semantic relationships</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Hybrid</td><td>Both</td><td>More setup</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0389","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-055-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"What does hybrid search need in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>A <strong>docstore</strong> (BM25 reads from it) plus a vector store created with <code>enable_hybrid=True</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0390","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-055-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"How do you install BM25 support and create a docstore for hybrid search?","a":"<p>Install <code>llama-index-retrievers-bm25</code>, then create a <code>SimpleDocumentStore</code> and add the documents.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># pip install llama-index-retrievers-bm25\nsmol_senpai_docstore = SimpleDocumentStore()\nsmol_senpai_docstore.add_documents(senpai_documents)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0391","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-055-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"How do you create a hybrid-enabled Qdrant vector store and storage context?","a":"<p>Pass <code>enable_hybrid=True</code> to <code>setup_vector_store</code> (Qdrant stores sparse and dense), then build a <code>StorageContext</code> from the docstore, index store and vector store.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>rr_fusion_vector_store = setup_vector_store(\n    QDRANT_URL, QDRANT_API_KEY, &quot;rr-fusion&quot;,\n    enable_hybrid=True          # Qdrant stores sparse + dense\n)\nrr_fusion_storage_context = StorageContext.from_defaults(\n    docstore=smol_senpai_docstore,\n    index_store=SimpleIndexStore(),\n    vector_store=rr_fusion_vector_store\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0392","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-055-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"How do you build the <code>VectorStoreIndex</code> for hybrid search?","a":"<p>Call <code>VectorStoreIndex.from_documents</code> with the storage context, so the docstore holds the nodes.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>index = VectorStoreIndex.from_documents(\n    documents=senpai_documents,\n    embed_model=Settings.embed_model,\n    storage_context=rr_fusion_storage_context,\n    transformations=[sentence_splitter, Settings.embed_model]\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0393","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-056-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"What are the <code>vector_store_query_mode</code> values in LlamaIndex?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>default</code></td><td>Pure dense vector search</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>hybrid</code></td><td>Vector + keyword search; <code>alpha</code> weights them (<code>alpha=0</code> gives BM25 only, <code>alpha=1</code> gives vector only)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>semantic_hybrid</code></td><td>Hybrid plus a semantic reranking step</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>sparse</code></td><td>Sparse vectors (mostly zeros, good for exact keywords/details); needs a sparse embedding model (e.g., FastEmbed <code>prithvida/Splade_PP_en_v1</code>) and <code>sparse_top_k</code> (nodes fetched from each of the sparse and dense queries)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>text_search</code></td><td>Exact keyword matches only</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0394","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-056-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"What is the difference between <code>similarity_top_k</code> and <code>hybrid_top_k</code>?","a":"<p><code>similarity_top_k</code> is the final node count after fusion. <code>hybrid_top_k</code> is the top-k for hybrid mode.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0395","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-056-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"What does the <code>alpha</code> value do in hybrid mode?","a":"<p>It weights vector against keyword search. <code>alpha=0</code> is BM25 only and <code>alpha=1</code> is vector only.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0396","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-056-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"How do you test different retrieval modes with a helper?","a":"<p>Call <code>as_retriever</code> with the mode kwargs, retrieve for a query and print each node's score and text.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def test_retrievers(query=QUERY_STRING, index=index, **kwargs):\n    retriever_engine = index.as_retriever(**kwargs)\n    retrieved_docs = retriever_engine.retrieve(query)\n    print(f&quot;Retrieved {len(retrieved_docs)} nodes.&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0397","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-056-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"What kwargs select the BM25-only, hybrid and text search modes in the test loop?","a":"<p>BM25: hybrid mode with <code>alpha</code> 0.0. Hybrid: hybrid mode with <code>alpha</code> 0.25. Text search: <code>text_search</code> mode with <code>similarity_top_k</code> 3.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>    &#x27;bm25&#x27;: {&#x27;vector_store_query_mode&#x27;: &#x27;hybrid&#x27;, &#x27;alpha&#x27;: 0.0, &#x27;hybrid_top_k&#x27;: 3},\n    &#x27;hybrid&#x27;: {&#x27;vector_store_query_mode&#x27;: &#x27;hybrid&#x27;, &#x27;alpha&#x27;: 0.25, &#x27;hybrid_top_k&#x27;: 3},\n    &#x27;text_search&#x27;: {&#x27;vector_store_query_mode&#x27;: &#x27;text_search&#x27;, &#x27;similarity_top_k&#x27;: 3},</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0398","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-057-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"What are the three steps of the hybrid fusion retriever (<code>QueryFusionRetriever</code>)?","a":"<p>(1) Create or rewrite several queries from the user query. (2) Retrieve with each query across an ensemble of retrievers. (3) Fuse and rerank.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0399","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-057-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"What is Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF)?","a":"<p>For each unique node, take 1/rank from every list it appears in, sum them, and reorder by that total. Nodes that rank consistently high across retrievers rise to the top, with no extra model or heavy computation (paper: Cormack et al., SIGIR 2009).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0400","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-057-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"What are the fusion <code>mode</code> options of <code>QueryFusionRetriever</code>?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Fusion <code>mode</code></th><th>How scores are combined</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>reciprocal_rerank</code></td><td>RRF; best general choice</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>relative_score</code></td><td>Min-max scale each retriever's scores to 0-1, weight per retriever, combine</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>dist_based_score</code></td><td>Like <code>relative_score</code> but scales using mean and standard deviation (less sensitive to outliers)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>simple</code></td><td>Reorder by original scores</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0401","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-057-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"How do you create a vector retriever and a BM25 retriever for fusion?","a":"<p>Use <code>index.as_retriever</code> for vectors and <code>BM25Retriever.from_defaults</code> with the docstore.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>vector_retriever = index.as_retriever(similarity_top_k=1)\nbm25_retriever = BM25Retriever.from_defaults(docstore=index.docstore, similarity_top_k=1)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0402","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-057-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"How do you create a <code>QueryFusionRetriever</code> with reciprocal rank fusion, and how do you disable LLM query generation?","a":"<p>Pass the retrievers with <code>mode=\"reciprocal_rerank\"</code>. Set <code>num_queries=1</code> to disable LLM query generation.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>retriever = QueryFusionRetriever(\n    [vector_retriever, bm25_retriever],\n    similarity_top_k=15,\n    num_queries=3,                 # set to 1 to disable LLM query generation\n    mode=&quot;reciprocal_rerank&quot;,\n    use_async=True,\n    verbose=True,\n    # query_gen_prompt=QUERY_GEN_PROMPT_TEMPLATE,\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0403","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-057-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"How do you turn a fusion retriever into a query engine?","a":"<p>Use <code>RetrieverQueryEngine.from_args</code> with a response mode and the QA template.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>rr_fusion_query_engine = RetrieverQueryEngine.from_args(\n    retriever,\n    response_mode=ResponseMode.COMPACT_ACCUMULATE,\n    use_async=True,\n    text_qa_template=HYPE_ANSWER_GEN_PROMPT_TEMPLATE\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0404","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-057-8-1-hybrid-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s043","q":"Why is BM25 plus vector search with reciprocal rank fusion worth using?","a":"<p>It is one of the most effective, cheapest upgrades to a RAG system.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0405","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-058-8-2-agentic-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s044","q":"What are data agents in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>LLM-powered workers that go beyond query engines. They read from static data and can also call external APIs and modify state.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0406","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-058-8-2-agentic-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s044","q":"What does a data agent need?","a":"<p>A <strong>reasoning loop</strong> and <strong>tool abstractions</strong>. Given a task, it decides which tools to call, in what order, with which parameters.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0407","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-058-8-2-agentic-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s044","q":"What does the agent do in the agentic RAG notebook, and what are the pieces?","a":"<p>It turns the user's question into <strong>metadata filters plus a query</strong> against the vector DB (auto-retrieval). The pieces are metadata on nodes (manual <code>known_for</code> plus extractors), a <code>VectorStoreInfo</code> describing the schema, a Pydantic schema for the tool arguments, a function tool, and an agent.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0408","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-058-8-2-agentic-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s044","q":"How are the extractors set up for the agentic RAG ingestion?","a":"<p>A <code>QuestionsAnsweredExtractor</code> with 2 questions and a <code>KeywordExtractor</code> with 5 keywords, then both go into the ingestion transformations.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>keyword_extractor = KeywordExtractor(keywords=5, llm=Settings.llm)\n\ntransformations = [sentence_splitter, qa_extractor, keyword_extractor, Settings.embed_model]\nnodes = ingest(documents=senpai_documents, transformations=transformations, vector_store=vector_store)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0409","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-058-8-2-agentic-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s044","q":"What is <code>VectorStoreInfo</code> used for in agentic RAG?","a":"<p>It tells the agent what metadata exists. The descriptions drive which filter the LLM picks.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0410","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-058-8-2-agentic-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s044","q":"How does the agent know which metadata field to use for each kind of input?","a":"<p>The <code>MetadataInfo</code> descriptions say so, for example <code>known_for</code> helps find the right thinker's words, <code>questions_this_excerpt_can_answer</code> is for when the user asks a question, and <code>excerpt_keywords</code> is for when the user submits keywords.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>MetadataInfo(name=&quot;known_for&quot;, type=&quot;str&quot;,\n             description=&quot;Useful for finding the right thinker&#x27;s words to answer a question.&quot;),\nMetadataInfo(name=&quot;questions_this_excerpt_can_answer&quot;, type=&quot;str&quot;,\n             description=&quot;Use this when the user asks a question.&quot;),\nMetadataInfo(name=&quot;excerpt_keywords&quot;, type=&quot;str&quot;,\n             description=&quot;Use this when the user submits keywords.&quot;),</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0411","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-058-8-2-agentic-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s044","q":"What is the Pydantic argument schema the LLM must fill in for the auto-retrieve tool?","a":"<p>A model with a <code>query</code> plus two lists of the same length: <code>filter_key_list</code> (metadata filter field names) and <code>filter_value_list</code> (their values). It is used with OpenAI function calling.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>class AutoRetrieveModel(BaseModel):\n    query: str = Field(..., description=&quot;A question the user wants to advice about&quot;)\n    filter_key_list: List[str] = Field(..., description=&quot;List of metadata filter field names&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0412","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-059-8-2-agentic-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s044","q":"How does the auto-retrieve function build filters from the LLM's choices?","a":"<p>It makes a <code>MetadataFilter</code> with the <code>CONTAINS</code> operator for each key and value pair.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>contains_filters = [\n    MetadataFilter(key=k, value=v, operator=FilterOperator.CONTAINS)\n    for k, v in zip(filter_key_list, filter_value_list)\n]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0413","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-059-8-2-agentic-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s044","q":"How does the auto-retrieve function retrieve with the filters?","a":"<p>It builds a hybrid <code>VectorIndexRetriever</code> with <code>alpha=0.65</code>, the filters and <code>top_k</code>, then wraps it in a query engine.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>retriever = VectorIndexRetriever(\n    index,\n    vector_store_query_mode=&quot;hybrid&quot;,\n    alpha=0.65,\n    filters=MetadataFilters(filters=contains_filters),\n    top_k=top_k\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0414","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-059-8-2-agentic-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s044","q":"How do you wrap the retrieve function as a tool and create the agent?","a":"<p>Use <code>FunctionTool.from_defaults</code> with the function, name, description and argument schema, then <code>OpenAIAgent.from_tools</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>auto_retrieve_tool = FunctionTool.from_defaults(\n    fn=auto_retrieve_fn,\n    name=&quot;words-of-senpai-info&quot;,\n    description=description,\n    fn_schema=AutoRetrieveModel\n)\nagent = OpenAIAgent.from_tools(tools=[auto_retrieve_tool], verbose=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0415","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-059-8-2-agentic-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s044","q":"Which metadata field does the agent tend to filter on for a full question, a \"find text that mentions\" prompt, and a named thinker?","a":"<p>A full question tends to filter on <code>questions_this_excerpt_can_answer</code>. A \"find text that mentions…\" prompt filters on <code>excerpt_keywords</code>. A named thinker filters on <code>author</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0416","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-059-8-2-agentic-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s044","q":"What do <code>AgentRunner</code> and <code>AgentWorker</code> do in the lower-level agent API?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>AgentRunner</code></td><td>Orchestrator: manages state (conversation memory), creates and maintains tasks, runs steps, exposes the chat interface</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>AgentWorker</code></td><td>Controls step-wise execution: given an input step, produces the next step; holds no state itself</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0417","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-059-8-2-agentic-rag","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s044","q":"How do you build an agent with the lower-level API?","a":"<p>Create a <code>FunctionCallingAgentWorker</code> from the tools, then wrap it in an <code>AgentRunner</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>agent_worker = FunctionCallingAgentWorker.from_tools(\n    [auto_retrieve_tool], llm=Settings.llm, verbose=True)\nagent_runner = AgentRunner(agent_worker, verbose=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0418","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-060-8-3-ensemble-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s045","q":"What is ensemble retrieval?","a":"<p>Try <strong>several retrieval strategies at once</strong> (here four chunk sizes), merge their results, and rerank.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0419","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-060-8-3-ensemble-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s045","q":"What are the steps of ensemble retrieval in LlamaIndex?","a":"<p>Build a vector index per strategy, wrap each retriever in an <code>IndexNode</code>, put the index nodes in a <code>SummaryIndex</code> (a simple list-based structure), use a <code>RecursiveRetriever</code> to fan the query out to every retriever, then rerank the combined nodes.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0420","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-060-8-3-ensemble-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s045","q":"How do you build one vector index per chunk size and track which strategy produced each node?","a":"<p>Split with each chunk size, store <code>chunk_size</code> in node metadata and exclude it from embedding and LLM text.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>chunk_sizes = [128, 256, 512, 1024]\n        node.metadata[&quot;chunk_size&quot;] = chunk_size                # track which strategy produced it\n        node.excluded_embed_metadata_keys = [&quot;chunk_size&quot;]\n        node.excluded_llm_metadata_keys = [&quot;chunk_size&quot;]\n    vector_indices.append(VectorStoreIndex(nodes))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0421","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-060-8-3-ensemble-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s045","q":"How do you wrap each retriever in an <code>IndexNode</code>?","a":"<p>Give each chunk size an id like <code>chunk_128</code>, create an <code>IndexNode</code> with that <code>index_id</code>, and map the id to the index's retriever.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>    node_id = f&quot;chunk_{chunk_size}&quot;\n    node = IndexNode(\n        text=(&quot;Retrieves relevant context from the Llama 2 paper (chunk size&quot; f&quot; {chunk_size})&quot;),\n        index_id=node_id,\n    )\n    retriever_nodes.append(node)\n    retriever_dict[node_id] = vector_index.as_retriever()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0422","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-060-8-3-ensemble-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s045","q":"Why does the index node text say \"Llama 2 paper\" in the ensemble retrieval notebook?","a":"<p>The notebook is adapted from the LlamaIndex docs. The wording is only a label.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0423","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-060-8-3-ensemble-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s045","q":"How do you create the root <code>RecursiveRetriever</code> over the summary index and the chunk-size retrievers?","a":"<p>Make a <code>SummaryIndex</code> from the retriever nodes, then pass its retriever as the root, together with the retriever dict.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>summary_index = SummaryIndex(retriever_nodes)\nretriever = RecursiveRetriever(\n    root_id=&quot;root&quot;,\n    retriever_dict={&quot;root&quot;: summary_index.as_retriever(), **retriever_dict},\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0424","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-060-8-3-ensemble-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s045","q":"How do you rerank the merged results of the ensemble retriever and synthesize an answer?","a":"<p>Create a <code>CohereRerank</code> postprocessor and pass it to <code>RetrieverQueryEngine</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>reranker = CohereRerank(top_n=5, api_key=CO_API_KEY)\nquery_engine = RetrieverQueryEngine(retriever, node_postprocessors=[reranker])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0425","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-060-8-3-ensemble-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s045","q":"How does reranking tell you which chunk-size strategy matters?","a":"<p>Compute the reciprocal rank of the first node from each chunk size in the final ranking. A higher MRR means that chunk size tends to rank earlier, so it is more relevant. In the demo, chunk size 128 ranked highest.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0426","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-060-8-3-ensemble-retrieval","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s045","q":"How does the <code>mrr_all</code> function compute MRR for each metadata value?","a":"<p>It finds the first position of each value in the ranked source nodes and sets MRR to <code>1 / (idx + 1)</code>, or 0 if absent.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def mrr_all(metadata_values, metadata_key, source_nodes):\n    # source_nodes is a ranked list; find first position of each metadata value\n    value_to_mrr_dict = {}\n    for metadata_value in metadata_values:\n        mrr = 0\n        for idx, source_node in enumerate(source_nodes):\n            if source_node.node.metadata[metadata_key] == metadata_value:\n                mrr = 1 / (idx + 1)\n                break\n        value_to_mrr_dict[metadata_value] = mrr\n    return pd.DataFrame(value_to_mrr_dict, index=[&quot;MRR&quot;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0427","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-061-8-4-ensemble-query-engine","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s046","q":"What is an ensemble query engine?","a":"<p>It runs <strong>several query engines</strong> (top-k vector, keyword table, knowledge graph and so on) and lets an LLM <strong>rate each result's relevance and synthesize</strong> one answer.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0428","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-061-8-4-ensemble-query-engine","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s046","q":"What are the steps to build an ensemble query engine?","a":"<p>Build indexes over the same nodes, create query engines with a QA prompt that asks for a relevance score, wrap each as a <code>QueryEngineTool</code> with a clear description, create a <code>RouterQueryEngine</code> with <code>LLMMultiSelector</code> (the LLM can pick more than one tool), and let <code>TreeSummarize</code> combine the answers.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0429","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-061-8-4-ensemble-query-engine","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s046","q":"What can a selector do in a router query engine?","a":"<p>Choose a data source, decide between summarization and semantic search, or combine multiple choices.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0430","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-061-8-4-ensemble-query-engine","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s046","q":"How do you build a keyword index and a vector index over the same nodes?","a":"<p>Add the nodes to a shared <code>StorageContext</code> docstore, then create <code>SimpleKeywordTableIndex</code> and <code>VectorStoreIndex</code> with that storage context.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>storage_context = StorageContext.from_defaults()\nstorage_context.docstore.add_documents(nodes)\n\nkeyword_index = SimpleKeywordTableIndex(nodes, storage_context=storage_context, show_progress=True)\nvector_index = VectorStoreIndex(nodes, storage_context=storage_context, show_progress=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0431","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-061-8-4-ensemble-query-engine","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s046","q":"What does the QA prompt of the ensemble query engine ask the LLM to add?","a":"<p>A relevance score for the answer, and to tell the user without making up an answer if the answer is not in the context.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0432","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-061-8-4-ensemble-query-engine","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s046","q":"How do you create the keyword and vector query engines with the scoring prompt?","a":"<p>Pass the prompt as <code>text_qa_template</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>keyword_query_engine = keyword_index.as_query_engine(text_qa_template=QA_PROMPT)\nvector_query_engine = vector_index.as_query_engine(text_qa_template=QA_PROMPT)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0433","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-062-8-4-ensemble-query-engine","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s046","q":"How are the keyword and vector query engines described as tools?","a":"<p>The keyword tool is for finding documents based on keywords and incomplete thoughts. The vector tool is for fully-formed questions.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>keyword_tool = QueryEngineTool.from_defaults(\n    query_engine=keyword_query_engine,\n    description=&quot;Useful for answering finding documents based on keywords and incomplete thoughts from a user.&quot;,\n)\nvector_tool = QueryEngineTool.from_defaults(\n    query_engine=vector_query_engine,\n    description=&quot;Useful for answering fully-formed questions from a user.&quot;,\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0434","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-062-8-4-ensemble-query-engine","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s046","q":"What does the tree summarize prompt of the ensemble query engine tell the LLM?","a":"<p>Context from multiple places is given and each part may have a relevance score. Answer the question from that context, and if the answer is not in the context, inform the user without making up an answer.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0435","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-062-8-4-ensemble-query-engine","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s046","q":"How do you create the <code>TreeSummarize</code> combiner?","a":"<p>Pass a <code>PromptTemplate</code> as <code>summary_template</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>tree_summarize = TreeSummarize(summary_template=PromptTemplate(TREE_SUMMARIZE_PROMPT_TMPL))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0436","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-062-8-4-ensemble-query-engine","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s046","q":"How do you create the <code>RouterQueryEngine</code> with <code>LLMMultiSelector</code>?","a":"<p>Pass the selector, the tools and the summarizer.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query_engine = RouterQueryEngine(\n    selector=LLMMultiSelector.from_defaults(),\n    query_engine_tools=[keyword_tool, vector_tool],\n    summarizer=tree_summarize,\n    verbose=True,\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0437","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-062-8-4-ensemble-query-engine","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s046","q":"How does the router behave for a fully formed question vs keyword-style input?","a":"<p>A fully formed question makes the router lean on the vector engine. Keyword-style input makes it lean on the keyword engine.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>response = await query_engine.aquery(&quot;specific knowledge, build wealth, achieve happiness?&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0438","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-062-8-4-ensemble-query-engine","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s046","q":"How do ensemble retrieval, ensemble query engine and <code>RouterQueryEngine</code> compare?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Technique</th><th>What it does</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Ensemble retrieval</td><td>Several retrievers (e.g., chunk sizes) + reranker</td><td>Comparing strategies, finding the best chunk size</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Ensemble query engine</td><td>Several query engines + LLM router and summarizer</td><td>Choosing the best strategy per query</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>RouterQueryEngine</code></td><td>LLM picks one or more tools from their descriptions</td><td>Dynamic tool selection</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0439","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-063-llamaindex-evaluation-module","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s047","q":"What does the built-in LlamaIndex evaluation module offer?","a":"<p>It is found in the docs under Advanced Topics, then Evaluation. It supports <strong>component-wise</strong> evaluation (the query engine without retrieval) and <strong>end-to-end</strong> evaluation (the whole system, multiple metrics). Metrics are mostly implemented as LLM-as-a-Judge calls.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0440","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-064-comparative-analysis-of-rag-techniques-a","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s048","q":"What is the ARAGOG paper?","a":"<p><em>ARAGOG: Advanced RAG Output Grading</em>. It compared RAG techniques with LlamaIndex abstractions.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0441","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-064-comparative-analysis-of-rag-techniques-a","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s048","q":"What data and statistical method did ARAGOG use?","a":"<p>423 arXiv papers on AI and LLMs, with 107 QA pairs (written by GPT-4, human validated). The detailed analysis used 13 papers plus noisy extras. It ran each technique 10 times for statistical reliability (ANOVA, then Tukey HSD for pairwise comparisons).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0442","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-064-comparative-analysis-of-rag-techniques-a","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s048","q":"Which metrics and techniques did ARAGOG compare?","a":"<p>Metrics: <strong>retrieval precision</strong> (0-1, relevance of retrieved context) and <strong>answer similarity</strong> (0-5, match to the reference answer). Techniques: sentence window retrieval, document summary index, HyDE, multi-query, MMR, Cohere reranker and LLM reranker.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0443","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-064-comparative-analysis-of-rag-techniques-a","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s048","q":"What were the ARAGOG results?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Best retrieval precision and answer similarity</td><td><strong>HyDE + LLM reranking</strong></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Strong, but inconsistent answer similarity</td><td>Sentence window retrieval</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Moderate</td><td>Document summary index, multi-query</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Lower</td><td>MMR, Cohere reranker</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"rag-llamaindex-f0444","card":"q-rag-llamaindex-064-comparative-analysis-of-rag-techniques-a","sec":"rag-llamaindex-s048","q":"What are the takeaways from the ARAGOG comparison?","a":"<p>Prioritize retrieval precision, because it drives faithfulness. Answer similarity also depends on the LLM and prompting, not only retrieval. A reasonable baseline is HyDE + LLM reranking. Use sentence window retrieval for precision-critical cases. Combine hybrid search, reranking and query transformation. Evaluate with repeated runs and significance tests. Faithfulness needs the LLM to understand retrieved meaning, not just match keywords.</p>","hand":true}];
